A black box in your car?
While American road designers are trying to find the money to repair the scattering system of highways, many are starting to see the solution in a small black box neatly attached to the dashboard of your car.
These devices, which track every mile passing by a motorbian and transmitting this information to officials, are at the center of a controversial attempt to modernize an obsolete system for the financing of American motorways undertaken by the planning bodies of Washington and the state.
Typically a boa bosoot planning arena unexpectedly spawned an intensive debate and colostic alliances.
Libertarians have acceded to environmental groups in lobbying granting the government the right to use small drawers to track the number of miles passed by by you and even perhaps where you are passing — and then using that information when compiling tax bills.
Tea drinking is in shock.
The American Civil liberties Union is also deeply concerned and raises a number of questions about privacy.
And although Congress can not yet reach an agreement, continue or not, a few states are not going to wait.
They are conceiving how within the next decade you can proceed to a system in which the drivers pay for every mile of the road that they pass.
Thousands of motorcyclists have already taken these black c boxes for testing, some of which have the function of satellite tracking.
This is really necessary for our country.
“This isn’t a matter on which we can have the right to choose,” said Hassan Ihirata, Executive Director of the Association of Governments of Southern California, who is preparing plans to start tracking the state of the miles passed by every Californian motor driver by 2025.
There will be changes in the way we pay these taxes.
There’s already technology for this.
Necessity is exacerbated by availability of funds from the Government Road Construction Fund, financed from taxes that Americans pay at gas stations.
Americans don’t buy as much gasoline as they used to.
Cars pass more than a gallon per gallon.
The federal tax itself, 18.4 ppm per gallon, hasn’t increased for 20 years.
Politicians do not want to increase the tax even per cent at high petrol prices.
“A tax on petrol simply cannot be preserved,” said Li Mannich, a transport policy expert at Minnesota University.
In its state, it was recently installed on the cars of 500 tracking devices to test a commile payment system.
"It will be the best alternative in the long run," he said.
Bounts call it a commemorative user license.
Unsurprisilantly, this idea attracts urban liberals, because with the help of taxes it will be possible to change the nature of trips to reduce the congestion of roads and greenhouse gas emissions, for example.
Planning authorities in California are looking into this system during the development of strategies to achieve the targets set by the ambitious laws of this state to combat global warming.
However, House member Bill Schuster (Recenaisant, Pennsylvania), chairman of the chamber's transport committee, said that he also sees the system as the most resilient long-lasting alternative.
Reaxon’s Free Market Adherents are also delighted to make drivers pay for every mile.
“It’s not just a tax that goes into a black hole,” said Adrian Moore, Vice President of Political Affairs.
People directly pay for what they receive.
This movement is also backed up by two former U.S. transport ministers who in 2011 called on Congress to move towards surfactories.
The U.S. U.S. Senate approved a $90-million-dollar Pitrige Pilot Project last year, involving about 10 000 cars.
However, the leaders of the house of representatives rejected this proposal due to the concerns of rural legislators, representing voters who in everyday life often have to pass many miles to get to work or to the city.
Several states and cities, however, go along this path on their own.
The greatest enthusiment is manifested in the state of Oregon, where 5000 drivers are involved to participate in the largest experiment in the country.
These drivers will soon pay the state for mushies instead of a tax on gasoline.
In Nevada, the pilot project has already been completed.
In New York, it is being considered.
Illinois will test it on a limited basis with the participation of trucks.
And the I-95 coalition, which includes the transportation departments of the 17 states of the eastern coast (including Maryland, Pennsylvania, Virgínament, and Florida), is studying how these changes.
This concept has not been universally recognized.
In Nevada, where about 50 volunteer vehicles were recently equipped with these devices, the drivers were concerned that the government could track every move.
“Concervicience about ‘big similums’ is a great problem,” said Alauddin Khan, head of strategy and efficiency management at the Nevada Department of Transport.
It wasn’t what people wanted.
When the tests went in full swing, the branch of the American Civil Liberties Union in Nevada warned on its website: “It will not be dae diligible to turn these devices into full-blown trampolines.”
There is no need to create a huge, cumbersome technological infrastructure, which will inevitably be expanded for storing entries about the day-to-to-tangible movements of individual citizens.
Nevada is one of a number of states that has a difficult search for low-cost technology, which would allow the state authorities to take into account passing miles, but without information about the place and time.
If you are able to do this, Hahn said, society will feel more relaxed.
Looking for this technology led some state agencies to a small young company in California called True Mileage.
Initially, this company was not engaged in assistance in the collection of state taxes.
It aspired to enter the emerging market of the type of car insurance, in which drivers pay on a mushroom basis.
But the devices that it is testing involve road designers because they don’t use GPS and provide a limited amount of information periodically uploaded via modem.
"People will be more inclined to do this if you don't keep trampling their speed and tracking their location," said Ryan Morrison, chief executive of True Mileage.
There have been a number of great bugs in some of these state pilot programs.
There are much less expensive and less obsessive ways to do this.
In Oregon, the designers are experimenting with the provision of various options to drivers.
They can choose the device with or without GPS.
Or they can completely abandon the device, deciding instead to pay a fixed fee based on the average number of miles, which all residents of the state pass.
In other places they hope to smash an idea of wary public, forcing the devices to do more, rather than less.
In New York, transport officials are aiming to develop a tidal device that will also accept payment on parking meters, provide “fees like you drive” insurance, and collect real-time frequency data pool from other drivers that motorists could use to avoid traffic junctions.
“Automobilists will involve the benefits that will be offered to them”, – stated in the document of urban planning design.
Some designers of the transport systems, however, are wondering whether everyone is talking about a blambile payment is simply a huge distraction.
According to the San Francisco-Civrose Traffic Commission, officials say that Congress could very easily overcome the bankruption of the trust fund for the construction of highways, raising taxes on petrol, raising taxes on gasoline.
An additional lump-to-equity or an annual tax could be levied on hybrid car drivers and others whose vehicles don’t use a lot of gasoline to pay their fair share.
“There’s no need for a radical surgical intermittance when all you have to do is accept aspirin,” said Randy Röntschler, director of the Commission on Legislature and Public Relations.
If we do this, hundreds of millions of drivers will be worried about their private life and a variety of other things.
The EU is preparing measures to support Ukraine in the event of economic pressure of Russia
The European Union has a reserve plan to provide Ukraine with gas, as well as to reach an agreement with the IMF on an emergency loan, if Russia takes any measures in response to the possible signing of an association agreement between the EU and Ukraine at the Vilnius summit.
Negotiations are being negotiated on a stand-by loan, and another EU official, directly involved in the negotiations, added that their goal is to conclude an agreement in the near future.
At the same time, in addition to a potential loan from the IMF, Ukraine can receive 610 million euros from the European Union itself.
Analysts, interviewed by Reuters, doubt that Ukraine and the IMF are able to overcome long-standing disagreements about the conditions of financing.
Do not believe in the possibility of the reforms necessary to receive the assistance, and the international rating agency S&P, which lowered Ukraine’s sovereign rating by one notch on Friday - to "B" from "B".
However, representatives of the EU say that the IMF can show flexibility in terms of lending, taking into account the circulpability of Ukraine.
In addition to the plan of financial support of the country, the EU has a reserve option to provide Ukraine with gas, the vast majority of whose deliveries are now coming from Russia.
Perhaps this will be gas from the “Northern stream” or a reverse from Slovakia.
The latter, according to the officials, is the most possible and acceptable way in the event that Russia “insulates” Ukraine.
Analyst analysts believe that this method of reversible supplies to Ukraine can only be used for a few weeks, and is likely to lead to a decrease in supplies to other regions.
Negotiations are being held between the EU countries and Ukrainians about how to create favorable conditions so that Ukraine can import gas from other sources, and not out of Russia, or from the same source, but on other routes.
Russia is outside the struggle for pollution of cities with cars
Attempts to solve the transport problems of large cities were observed in most megacities of the world since the second half of the twentieth century.
As a rule, we are talking either about their reconfiguration and expansion of highways, or about attempts to reduce the demand for car trips, the number of cars and the time of their use.
There is a well-relored example of Singapore, which introduced a strict quota of the increase in the number of private cars, and the right of their acquisition is bought at auction.
Its price can be two to three times the price of the car.
European cities, such including London, have imposed an entrance fee to the city center.
In Germany, for example in Hamburg and Stuttgart, the so-called green zones are administered, where only cars with a certain eco-class are allowed to enter, which also uses high-quality fuels (including biofuels or electric cars).
The Agency for Environmental Protection of Beijing, for example, in 2012 approved a “five-Yocary clean air plan” with a total value of about 250 billion yubans (about $ 40 billion).
As told “Kommersant” the Director of the Department for the control of transport pollution of the municipal Bureau of environmental protection of Beijing, the main goal of the five-year-onrise is to reduce leading air polluters by 20-35% by 2017, an increase in the number of private cars to a level not exceeding 6 million (now 5.2 million), as well as an increase of not more than 5% of the use of fuel per vehicle.
According to the Agency, now motor transport in Beijing is responsible for 22.5% of total air pollution.
Among the main measures of the program - limiting the use of road transport, as well as the introduction of additional taxes for car holders.
Among other things, the urban measures of “green five-methenium” include an accelerated transition compared with the rest of the country to European fuel standards, the introduction of a local system of eco-standards and marking of cars and fuel, the restriction on the entry of cars into the central part of the city, a ban on the use of obsolete vehicles (in addition, the creation of encouraging financial programs for the replacement of old cars with hybrid or electric vehicles), the development of electric vehicles (including public transport).
Among the automobile innovations of Beijing also includes a ban for all private cars on traffic within the fifth transport ring (together in the capital of the People's Republic of the People's Republic of China, one day per week (relevant information is contained in a vehicle number), as well as the issuance of registration plates for lottery-based cars (for example, in 2011, the first year of the lottery, the total number of permits for the registration of private cars in Beijing accounted for only a third of the number).
In accordance with the current state program "Environmental protection for 2012-2020", the number of cities with high and very high air pollution should be reduced to 128 (in 2012 there were 138).
According to the Ministry of Natural Resources, in 2011, “mobility sources” accounted for 41% of all emissions of polluting substances in the atmosphere of cities.
In Moscow, for example, the emissions from cars are ten times higher than industrial, and in St. Petersburg - nine times.
In the Russian Federation so far only begin to think about the possibility of restrictive regulation of cars on the streets of cities.
Mikhail Blinkin, the Director of the Institute of Transport and Transport Politics of HSE Mikhail Blinkin believes that administrative and fiscal measures aimed at suppressing the demand for car trips is obviously unpopular, they can be taken by society only with their complete universality.
In the case of Moscow there is a unique problem associated with the structure of its car park, where there are two clusters who are weakly sensitive to any regulatory influence - official and personal cars, as well as cars of "privileged" users, the total number of which is at least 200 thousand (about 5% of the total number of cars in Moscow).
Recently, urbanists from the ECOM center in St. Petersburg have prepared a study, which analyzes the balance of urban areas between residential development, road surface area and the number of vehicles.
The main conclusions of the researchers: the center of the city is provided with roads by two times as required, and the majority of motorists living in the center do not use cars every other day, leaving them for a long time in parking lots or just on the streets.
As a result, it is proposed to build not parking, but car storks, not to expand, but to reduce the roadway (in order that the streets become more friendly for pedestrians), as well as to limit the use and placement of personal transport within the territory of the protected area of the historical center (a common territory of about 3212 hectares, covering a number of central districts of the city).
Fines for unsanctioned street trading in Vologda will grow significantly
According to the city authorities, an increase in the amount of fines will help to restore order in Vologda and liberate the streets from spontaneous tents and trays.
The majority of street merchants do not pay the taxes, the products that they sell, often do not pass adequate sanitary control.
And this means that the health is at the same level.
So, the lower limit of a fine for citizens for unsanctioned trade from November will increase by six times - from 500 rubles to 3000 rubles, the press service of the Vologda Administration reports.
Starman Sachs warned about the risks for the Russian economy
Goldman Sachs has warned about the growing risks for the main driver of fragile economic growth in Russia - consumption.
This is, first of all, the crisis of non-payment for unsecured consumer loans and massive reductions of workers.
Our main concern now is not that growth has subsided, but rather the structure of this growth.
In recent years, it is completely conditioned by the consumption, which almost does not reduce turnover, ”said Clemens Grafe, chief economist of Goldman Sachs for Russia, presenting yesterday the quarterly report of the investment bank on the Russian economy.
Now the nominal increase in wages in Russia - about 10%.
With inflation of 6%, it will be able to ensure future consumer demand at about the current level, Goldman Sachs is expected.
But the profitability of Russian companies is falling, therefore, most likely, they will be engaged in optimizing personnel costs.
Today we see a significant increase in the share of wages in GDP: if wages are growing by 10%, then the GDP is only by 2 per cent.
Companies faced a decrease in profitability.
If it doesn’t grow, it can lead to redundancies and an increase in unemployment.
The Russian business can not raise the salaries of the Russian business, comments the chief economist of Barclays Capital for Russia and the CIS Vladimir Pantyushin.
Unemployment is close to historical minimums, competition for employees is high.
To lure employees from the outside or to keep the current, employers have to raise salaries.
Consumption in Russia is supported by a very rapid increase in consumer lending.
According to Mr. Grafe, due to the extremely high interest rates on consumer loans, this type of lending does not have a multiplicative effect on the country’s economy.
“We did not see any benefits for the economy from the growth of consumer lending, the money does not diverge on the economy, but returned to the same banks in the form of interest payments,” the economist said.
But the problem is the other - Goldman Sachs expect an overdue overdue unsecured loans.
They are taken mainly by poor people who have nothing to provide for security.
Percentage on such loans is high.
As a result, they are more often not returned, ”said Mr. Grafe.
Therefore, the second  Threat to the growth of the economy in Russia - a possible crisis of non-payment for unsecured loans.
Vasily Solodkov, the Director of the HSE’s Banking Institute, now sees signs of a brewing banking crisis.
Small lending organizations, without having access to cheap resources that state-owned banks have, were forced to raise funds of the population at high-interest.
In response, state-owned banks were on the path of the war and began to reduce credit rates, the economist continues.
Small credit institutions can not issue loans at the same interest, otherwise they will have a negative interest margin.
If state-owned banks do not renounce dumping, Russia faces a full-fledged banking crisis, says Vasily Solodkov.
Deprivation of licenses of a number of banks in recent weeks the economist considers the harbinger of a mass collapse.
“The state-owned banks themselves will not be able to cope with such a situation: the deposit insurance system was initially not designed for a systemic crisis”, – warns the head of the Institute.
But the growth of consumption will slow down without a crisis of non-pluses, according to the investment bank - due to the refusal to index the salaries of civil servants laid down in the current version of the draft budget.
Partictically, the blow to the consumption will be mitigated by the froze tariffs of natural monopolies (and, as a result, a decrease in inflation).
But only partially: if the investment does not grow (and there are no prerequisites for this at the time - see the certificate), the growth of consumption will still be slowed down, Goldman Sachs is sure.
Vladimir Pantyushin from Barclays Capital does not yet see presupconditions for the implementation of pessimistic scenarios.
“The main risk is still a fall in the price of the oil price,” he says.
According to his estimation, the economy of Russia will begin to decline at the cost of an oil below $ 90 / barrel.
Goldman Sachs also noted that the Central Bank is not yet able to reduce interest rates in the economy.
There is a paradoxical picture: inflation decreased, and banks began to raise rates.
This may mean that they didn’t believe the Central Bank, which announced the transition to targeting inflation,” Clemens Grafe said.
The policy of the Central Bank does not affect market rates, it also affects inter-bank lending rates.
“For the Central Bank, this is the collapse of all hopes,” Clemen Grafe said.
The money received at the auction of the Central Bank, the banks are used not for lending to the economy, but to manage their liquidity
As soon as the rate decreases, the foreign exchange rate immediately changes, this means that the funds are trying to leave for speculation against the ruble.
“Sooner or later, the Central Bank will understand that this strategy does not work,” Grafe said and reminded that the state plans to put the ruble in a “free voyage” by the end of 2015.
But you will either have to do this earlier, or raise the key rate of the Central Bank (5.5%), he said.
According to his estimation, the ruble exchange rate is now artificially overestimated by 10%.
The rubbream only one road - to get weaker, the expert draws infers.
But if the Central Bank plunders in financiers at least a shadow of doubt that the liquidation of the currency corridor is not a part of the ruble to weaken the ruble, this can bring the ruble much stronger.
In Chelyabinsk was held the II Congress of peoples of the Southern Urals.
The forum is timed to the Day of National Unity, the 400-anniversary of the restoration of Russian statehood and the 20-th anniversary of the adoption of the Constitution of Russia.
The Congress was attended by delegations from all cities and districts of the region, representatives of national and cultural associations, religious denouncing bodies, legislative and executive authorities - a total of about 350 people.
The course of the forum is aimed at strengthening inter-ethnic harmony.
Here we can show an example not only to other regions, but also to other countries.
We don’t have discrepanties or disagreements.
We are living in a complete mutual understanding”, – says Theophan, metropolitan of Chelyabinsk and Zlatoustovsky.
During the meeting, a number of issues were considered, including the upbringing of patriotism and cultural cooperation.
At the end of the congress, a resolution was adopted.
The unofficial part of the forum persisted in the theater of opera and ballet.
Here opened an exhibition of national and cultural ununions of the Chelyabinsk region.
Snowden is ready to “cooperate” with Germany on the U.S. intelligence
Edward Snowden, U.S. intelligence whistle revolver, said he was ready to go to Berlin to testify to the German parliament if the U.S. National Welfare and its director Keith Alsander won’t be able to answer questions about their activities.
German MP Hans-Christian Srushebe on Thursday met with Mr. Snowden in Russia, where he was granted asylum to discuss his testimonies in Germany.
In a letter from Mr. Snowden, which the deputy presented to the media in Berlin on Friday, said: “Although the result of my efforts was clearly positive, my government continues to treat dissatisfaction as treason and seeks to criminalize political statements with criminal accusations without any protection.”
Telling the truth isn’t a crime.
In the letter, Mr. Snowden said that he believed that the support of the international community could convince the U.S. government to renounce criminal charges against him.
Accusations filed by the U.S. Department of justice include espionage and property the theft.
Hans-Peter Friedrich, Germany’s interior minister, told Zeit Online: “If Mr. Snowden is ready to talk to German officials, we’ll find ways to make it possible.”
Relevance between the U.S.-H.E.S. became tense after claims that the NSA was tapped by Chancellor Angela Merkel’s phone.
Thomas Opperman, an MP who leads a parliamentary group overseeing the reconnaissance, said that if there is an opportunity to listen to Mr. Snowden as a whistleblower “without putting him at risk or destroying relations with the U.S. completely,” it must be used.
Mr. Strobele, a member of parliament from the German Green Party, has published his photo with Mr. Snowden on Twitter.
During the visit to Russia, he was accompanied by two German journalists.
Mr. Strobele was said that, according to the lawyer of the former NSA contractor, Snowden could not have returned to Russia if he had gone away.
If Mr. Snowden testimonized in Germany, he would need arguing that he would be “secure”, the deputy said.
Mr. Snowden said in a letter that he was confronted with a “harsevere and constant” campaign of persecution, which forced him to leave his home.
However, he said that he was enthusiastic about a global reaction to “his political statements.”
Citizens all over the world, as well as high-ranking officials – including in the United States – considered the excavation of an uncontrollable system pervasive spectacling for society.
The letter contains a proposal to cooperate with the German authorities, “when the difficulties of this humanitarian situation will be solved”.
Frontier Airlines will be charged for hand luggage
Frontier Airlines plans to levy up to $ 100 passengers for carrying hand luggage aboard its flight.
Frontier Airlines plans to start charging up to $ 100 for hand luggage and $2 for coffee or soda, although their ad on Wednesday stated that the passengers could keep the entire jar.
The new hand luggage fee applies to bags in the upper luggage compartments, so small bags placed under the seat will remain free of charge.
Frontier said it will charge $25 if the fee is paid in advance, and $100 if the travellers will pay only by getting to land.
Frontier representative Kate O'Malley said a fee of $ 100 should force the passengers to take care of payment in advance.
“We don’t want to charge for it,” she said.
Airlines began to charge fees for the first and second lubricated bag in 2008.
Passengers, trying to avoid these fees, fill as long as they can, in hand luggage placed in the upper luggage compartments, because of which these compartments often do not have enough space in these compartments.
Fees - one of the ways to force the passengers to carry less on board.
O'Malley said that this new collection isn't really to make money.
The fact is the fact that the Most Loyal Customers of Frontier say that it is becoming more and more and more difficult to find a place in the upper luggage compartments.
Passengers, who buy tickets on the airline's website, will do not have to pay.
This means that one passenger in the queue at an exit flight Frontier can be able to smash the bag for free, while the next passenger in queue can pay $ 100 for the same bag.
O’Malley said that the change of procedures on the website and the Frontier registration latpodes is designed to ensure that the passengers will be aware of the collection before they get to the landing.
Frontier’s new hand luggage collection will not begin to be levied until the summer, although the date hasn’t yet been established.
Passengers often cluttize baggage charges, but airlines advocate them.
They allege luggage processing costs money, and the passengers who need this service must pay for it.
On a Wall-Strait consider the addition of luggage charges a sign that airlines charge enough money to cover the cost of air travel after several years of losses.
However, most of them didn't apply for hand luggage.
Spirit Airlines Involves the machining for hand luggage three years ago, and another discuner Allegant Air later followed suit.
The only other airline with such a collection is the Hungarian Wizz Air, said airline consultant Jay Sørensen, who closely monitors additional fees.
According to his opinion in a report from December 2011, the fee for hand luggage brings Spirit $ 50 million a year.
Sorensen, the former top manager of Midwest Airlines, was recently flying a Spirit flight, and he was wondering what he’d find an approach when passengers collide with an unambiguous Spirit for hand luggage.
“The landing process was the windiest that I’ve ever seen during my career in airlines,” he said.
I was expecting to see a granny of the tooth teeth and the occurrence of a fight at the out-of-surrival.
the plane was full, he said, "and the landing went quickly."
Frontier also pees for Spirit with regard to a payment of $ 2 for coffee, tea, soda or soybeans.
Frontier stated that the passengers who receive soda or the junction can leave the entire jar and that the share of coffee will be provided free of charge.
She'll still distribute the water for free.
U.S. Airways briefly attempted to charge for a drink in 2008, but gave it up seven months after the passengers began to complain and no other large airline followed suit.
Frontier’s hand-course-feasure enrolment initiative when passengers don’t buy tickets directly from an airline is its latest job of attracting customers to their website.
Airlines pay online ticket sellers such as Orbitz from $10 to $25 for each ticket sold.
This gave all airlines an institient incentive to encourage passengers to buy tickets directly from them, and do not contact a tourist online agency.
However, Frontier went the farthest in this area.
In September, she began to give twice as much bonus similates of a frequently flying passenger to customers who bought tickets through an online travel agency.
On Wednesday, she craved a premium number of miles of up to 25 per cent of a trip.
So, a 1000-mile trip with Frontier, purchased from an online travel agency, would allow you to get 250 miles.
In addition, the passengers are able to choose a place in advance only if they buy tickets directly on the Frontier website.
Frontier has a database of loyal customers in her hometown of Denver, but her business is shrinking and becoming unprofitable.
Revenue decreased by 9%, and flight opportunities decreased by almost 13 percent in the first-twenty, according to a financial statement released Wednesday by the parent company Republic Airways Holdings Inc.
The Republic is trying to rectify Frontier’s finances as part of an airline.
NSA blames ‘interior buggy’ rather than hackers to shut down
Filled with a secrecy of the National Security Agency said on Friday night that the shutdown of their site for a few hours caused a technical malculation, and not hackers, as stated in the network.
“NSA.gov was unavailable for several o’clock this evening due to an internal error that occurred during the scheduled renovation,” the intelligence agency said in an official e-write.
The problem will be solved tonight.
Allegations that the interruption in the work was caused by a distributed denial-and-of-maintenance attack [DDoS] is unfaithful.
Earlier this evening, online server-monitoring systems recorded that the NSA website didn’t work for at least six Hours and the site is still unavailable for some users.
Earlier, the representative of the NSA told ABC News that the internal secrecy of the agency “does not” was hacked.
No classified information is in jeopardy, said the representative.
At least one online group of activist hackers stated that it is responsible for dismantling the NSA using a DDoS-attack.
DDoS attacks are designed so as to whipping the target site with traffic until the servers are overwhelmed and the site does not go out of order.
Haglooking tactics are relatively simple, and the attacks are not designed to penetrate the internal network of the target system.
Earlier, the ultra-secret NNB, once nicknamed “There Is No Such Agency,” found itself in recent months at the center of public attention and bitter critique after a series of revelations about her extensive surveillance programs abroad and at the country – it’s all a reaction to NSA secret files stolen from an agency and published by a dismasenged former NSA collaborator, Edward Snowden.
Grosting controversy around the agency has sparked talk that today’s incident was the result of purposeful actions by hackers.
Bombardier profit decreases with a drop in deliveries and the number of orders for airplanes
Bombardier Corporation, the Canadian manufacturer of aircraft and trains, reported on Thursday a reduction in net profit by 15 per cent due to a reduced number of orders and deliveries of aircraft in the third quarter and problems with contracts in its railway.
Bombardier, based in Montreal, also did not publish any data on the flight tests of its latest CSeries aircraft and did not provide new information as to whether ambitious plans will have been implemented to put the aircraft into commercial operation by the next St.
After the first flight of a prototype of an airborne aircraft about a year and a half ago, he flew only three more times, which raises questions about whether there is a stage of testing on schedule.
The results didn’t live up for forecasts and led to a drop in shares of more than plough of more than 8% on the Toronto Stock Exchange.
Cameron Doerksen, an analyst at the National Bank Financial, lowered on Thursday’s assessment from “above the market average” to “medi-driving” due to the belief that the growth of stocks is limited in the next quarter or two.
“Although the decrease in the number of deliveries of the aircraft was generally predictable, we are certainly disappointed with the profits of the transport department,” Doerksen said in a stock market review.
We believe that Bombardier will receive new CSeries orders as the flight test program continues.
Nevertheless, if new orders are not announced in the coming months, we anticipate that the market will become more skeptical of the program.
Bombardier hopes that the CSeries aircraft family will allow it to win a place in the lower-prior price segment of the market, which is now dominated by Boeing and Airbus.
The first prototype of the aircraft was presented in March and for the first time made a flight in September after several months of a delay.
However, CSeries firm orders are not too much – 177, as potential buyers are waiting for flight test results to check the company’s statements about the fuel efficiency and the potential economy of the new liner.
In total, there are now 403 orders and agreements with 15 customers and operators.
Chief CEO Pierre Bodouane was confident that Bombardier would reach its goal of 300 firm orders by the time the first aircraft was put into commercial operation.
On Thursday, the leaders also assured analysts and the media that the program is moving forward according to the plan.
“The test-fashioned aircraft didn’t stay on the ground for longer than it was expected,” Bedouan said during a phone conference, adding that ground tests and software upgrades were planned at the time of the plane’s downtime.
All manufacturers plan to test in a different manner.
We decided to spend the first flight and take a break for renovation, so we did.
This will be the case throughout the flight testing program.
The second of the five test specimulators should fly in the coming weeks and all the others will soon follow it, the company said.
Nevertheless, analysts are skeptical about the statement that the first client will be able to start operating the CSeries aircraft in 12 months after its first flight.
Bombardier said that it is estimating the date of commissioning and will provide new information for the next few months.
“This scourge of the flight test – at least, apparently, and is in accordance with Bombardier’s internal schedule – reinforces our point of view that the commissioning will be postponed for the first quarter of 2015,” Doerksen said.
In the third tranquish, which ended on Sept. on September 30, Bombardier's net income fell to $ 147 million or 8 cents per share, from $172 million per share last year.
Corrected earnings per share remained the same - 9 cents.
Grosfling income decreased slightly - from $ 4.2 to $ 4.1 billion.
Analysts were expecting a profit of 10 octopres per share and grolobe income of $4.56 billion, according to Thomson Reuters I/B/E/S
The world’s fourth-largest aircraft manufacturer reported that it has delivered 45 aircraft in a quarter, which is less than in the previous year - 57.
The total number of orders fell from 83 to 26 aircraft.
The portfolio of orders of the aerospace department amounted to $ 32.9 billion as of September 30, without a change from December 3.
“In the aerospace region, the results corresponded to our goals, but a small number of incoming orders and general market conditions became an unpleasant factor,” Bodouane said.
Grossiover in the aerospace direction fell by 13 percent to $ 2 billion.
Bombardier, the world’s largest manufacturer of trains, said that gross revenue in this sector has risen by almost 11 per cent to $2.1 billion.
The portfolio of orders in the transport unit amounted to $32.6 billion on September 30, which is slightly higher than on December 3.
The income of the transport unit was adversely affected by the problems with the implementation of several major contracts.
The management said that a new development plan will be presented in the fourth Quarter.
The shares of Bombardier, which also announced that Google’s chief financial officer Patrick Pichett will join the board of directors, fell 8.5 per cent to C $ 4.83 at auction in the middle of Thursday.
The Brazilian company Embraer SA, the world's third-largest commercial aircraft maker and the closest competitor to Bombardier, said on Thursday a decrease in quarterly revenue by 10 per cent.
Sony Expects a Lower Annual Profit
The Japanese manufacturer of electronics, the corporation, Sony, having completed the last quarter with a net loss of 19.3 billion yen, or $ 197 million, reduced the forecast for profit for the current fiscal year.
The results of Sony for the period from July to September 2013 turned out to be more depressing than expected, which is due to a drop in demand for televisions, video cameras and personal computers manufactured by a Japanese corporation.
The television business of Sony in the second quarter brought the company's first operating profit in a three-eavial profit of 5.2 billion yen, in the reporting period again fell again to 9.3 billion yen of operating loss.
The Japanese market of consumer electronics is experiencing difficult times, especially due to a decrease in the demand for televisions.
And while the competitors seek to look for a way out of the difficult situation, Sony continues to concentrate on the consumer segment.
For example, one of the main competitors of Sony, Panasonic Corporation, has recently shifted the emphasis on industrial components: here the company's sales are growing at a high pace, especially due to automotive systems and environmentally friendly technologies.
As a result by the end of the financial year, which will end in March 2014, Sony expects to receive 179 billion yen of operating profit against the previously expected 230 billion yen.
At the same time, according to Thomson Reuters, analysts assumed that this figure will be much higher and will amount to 221 billion yen.
Striving to get out of the crisis, Sony is expanding the product line.
In the middle of this month was announced the start of sales of “smart “smart” hours from the Japanese corporation, endowed with a number of fashionable functions that will allow you to get out of your smartphone 100 times a day.
After Sony lowered the annual forecast for profit and revenue, the company's shares in the morning at the in the morning at the inauguration in Tokyo lost more than 11%, dropping to 1668 yen per share.
Speech gene turned out to be stimulant of synapse formation
Scientists from Johns Hopkins University and the Mount Sinai Medical School have discovered a squirrel, thanks to which Foxp2 Speech gene performs its own function, stimulating the formation of new connections between neurons.
The study is published in Science, you can read its short content on the website of the journal.
The Foxp2 gene is the first well-released gene, whose function is directly related to speech.
To establish his role in 2001 thanks to the discovery of a family from several people who could not correctly pronounce the words and sometimes did not even understand each other themselves.
Scientists figured out that in family members was impracticated the work of the Foxp2 gene, however, how it performs its function, it was not yet known.
In a new study, biologists have shown that at least part of their functions, Foxp2 performs as a stimulant to form new synapses in the area associated with the formation of speech.
It performs this thanks to a different gene, SRPX2.
The latter was discovered as a result of finding factors that stimulate synapses.
SRPX2 turned out to be one out of 10 such genes found by the authors, while only on its activity Foxp2.
What SRPX2 really affects wocasticalization, the scientists have confirmed in an experiment on mice.
When in the animals gene activity was artificially depreciated, they cried less when divided with the mother.
If the activity of the gene was repaired, the frequency of sounds produced was also recovered.
Previously, the mice also showed a connection with the vocalization of Foxp2.
The animals, who introduced a human recognition of the gene, squeezed more actively and at a lower frequency than ordinary mice.
Until now, however, scientists don’t know whether the work of Foxp2 is associated and, accordingly, SRPX2 controlled with purely “mechanical” properties for the formation of sounds or more subtle processes.
Cocine Dependence Lawyer Who Warns the Leader of a Criminal Entity About the Police Expulsion Is Imprisoned in Jail
42-year-old Basharat Ditta transferred information to the criminal authority Neil Scarborough
Advocacy was afraid that his clandestine narcotic dependence will be revealed
Sentenced to three years in prison by the Liverpool royal court.
Prestigious lawyer, who told the drug lord about a major police investigation, because he was afraid of exposing his secrecy of narcotic dependence, was imprisoned for three years.
Basharat Ditta, 42-year-old, handed the criminal authority Neil Scarborough classified information about the investigation of his activities on drug trafficking after being threatened by his cocaine addiction.
The lawyer, who was nicknamed Bash and dubbed a “cool lawyer among the criminals”, was arrested at his home in 2011 after a co-investigation for Scarborough, whom he presented earlier at a drug-driversed court.
The officers spotted how 32-year-old Scarborough left three bags of cocaine outside a lawyer’s house in Blackburn, Lancashire, while he was at the dinner association of jurists with his colleagues.
The investigation revealed that Ditta “regularly used” the drug of class A, after tests showed traces of cocaine in his hair, on his wallet and on credit cards.
For eight months from January to August 2011, he tried to illegally receive information about the arrests of two people on behalf of Scarborough, as well as his accomplice.
All four of the suspects at the same time were monitored by police as part of a large-scale investigation into a criminal organization selling heroin and cocaine in Lancashire, Cumbria, Merciside, Berkshire and West Yorkshire.
They and another 32 others were later jailed after the police confiscated in a series of heroin and co-coffee raids worth £1.5 million, as well as more than £200,000 in cash.
Diet, the 42-year-old passed information to criminals for the fear that his cocaine addiction will be revealed.
Today, at the Liverpool Royal Court of Diet, which works for the law firm Forbes Solicitors, located in Blackburn, was captivated after admitting his guilt on two occasions to deliberately obstruct the pursuit of justice following a three-week court at the Liverpool Crown Court.
He pleaded for coca covalence at a previous trial.
The lawyer’s unvelopment took place after Scarboro’s collaborating police found that he had regularly spoken to Diet on the phone since February 2011.
Two detective investigators followed the suspect and found how he approached Diet’s house in Blackburn and placed drugs of 60 percent purity in a black golf gird girdle under the garbage cans of a lawyer.
Shortly after Scarborough's transfer, Scarboro repeatedly referred to Diet, who was at a dinner at Ewood Park's Blackburne Rovers.
The lawyer returned to home for drugs; there were nine conversations between them.
The court found that Ditta “regularly used cocaine” after the tests found traces of a class A drug in his hair, purse and on his credit cards.
Ditta was later Arrested, but denies cocaine use, said he was talking to a suspected dealer because he was his client and insisted that their communication constituted a “lawyer’s secrecy”.
During his detention, Ditta took his wallet and tried to retrieve several credit cards, but they were all confiscated, he was also taken a hair sample.
During an interrogation in the police, he said that, along with the workplace, he had a home office and clients came to his house on legal affairs.
However, it became known to the court that after important arrests, he called the largest participants in drug trafficking, a number of whom he previously represented in the court to tell what detectives know about them.
Anne White said: “If someone knows that you shouldn’t break the law, it’s a criminal lawyer.”
Mr. Dietta is accused of abusing his position as a criminal lawyer, since he has entered into too close relations with certain clients.
The contact that we are talking about is not just a narcotic drug dealer, but a narcotic trader who supplies his own lawyer.
Some of his conversations, of course, will certainly turn out legitimate, since he was their lawyer.
However, this largely shifted the boundaries of the usual relations between the lawyer and the client.
He obstructed a police investigation as strongly as possible to allow these persons to continue their criminal activities.
Mr. Ditta didn't revere his profession, he disgraced it.
He became too close to specific customers, in particular Scarborough, and allowed him to question his disinterest.
Ditta pleaded not guilty and said: “If I was a corrupt lawyer that I’m not, and I’d like to provide information to Mr. Scarborough, I wouldn’t have waited 15 hours, I’d have done it immediately.”
But after the meeting, Senior Officer Lee Halstead from Lancashire police said, “Mr. Ditta turned from a criminal lawyer into a criminal offender as soon as he began to purchase drugs from organized crime.”
His predicate cocine has made him hopelessly compromised and vulnerable to those of major members of the criminal groups, who indcriminated him to obtain valuable information about police investigations.
Advoclaries should follow the highest standards of professional ethic and instill confidence in society.
Mr. Ditta betrayed this trust and tried to hide his profession.
The investigation of Mr. Ditt was conducted by the Lancashire unit on a particularly dangerous organized crime, which has already reached his sentence in three coco-plus storing and, now to prevent the administration of justice, demonstrating our desire to achieve a fair punishment for criminals.
Let this case serve as a warning to the criminals that no one is beyond the reach of the law.
We will find you and bring you to justice.
Scarboro himself was sentenced to 14 years after admitting his guilt in conspiring to supply heroin, cocaine and marijuana.
A total of 35 persons who participated in the machinations were sentenced to 153 years for drug-related crimes.
On his website, Ditta arranged a conversation in the form of questions and answers, in which he says that the work of his dreams is a lawyer representing clients with a death sentence in America, an ideal companion for him at a dinner - Mohammed Ali, and the motivation to work is inequality.
Stadium in Yaroslavl is not ready to receive 22 thousand spectators, said the police, who were present today at the meeting of the RFU CDC.
The flight program is overestimated, in their opinion, about two times.
During the match of the 1/16 final of the Cup of Russia with “Spartacus” was involved only a thousand stewards with a regular norm of nine thousand.
Spartak fans relied on 2,200 places, that is, 10 percent of the capacity of the stadium, however, in an agreement with the Moscow club, they were sold 5 thousand tickets.
This data was announced by the head of the CDC Artur Grigoryants.
The U.S. eavescive Japanese high-ranking officials
On Friday, November 1, one of the representatives of the American special services, who preferred not to reveal his name, stated that the United States was eavesdropping on telephone conversations of high-ranking Japanese officials.
This person has confirmed that there are several dots designed for listening in the country of the Rising Sun.
At the same time he noted that the United States, Great Britain, Australia, Canada, New Zealand do not conduct reconnaissance activities against each other.
According to him, this happened during the Second world war, when these countries were allies.
But now Japan, like Germany, despite allied relations with the Americans in the post-war period, are facilities for reconnaissance activities, NHK TV channel reported.
Officially, none of the parties has not yet commented on this information.
We will remind, the news about the surveillance of US special special services for the Chancellor of Germany appeared last week.
According to German journalists, the NSA may have tapped Merkel's phone for the last ten years.
The chancellor herself, according to some reports, took the news about her wiretapping very painfully.
She said that the allies, in her opinion, are Germany and the U.S. for decades, such an observation of the head of the government is unacceptable.
In the meantime, Edward Snowden said that he is ready to share the details about the eavesdropping of Angela Merkel's telephone conversations with employees of the German prosecutor's office.
The German deliberately flew to Moscow to meet a former CIA employee.
Bashkortosa can put a grain for auction no earlier than the beginning of 2014
Bashkortostan in the course of state procurement interventions can put grain for auction no earlier than in the beginning of 2014, said the Minister of agriculture of the Republic Nikolai Kovalenko.
To this day, the market prices are such that they do not stimulate sales in an interventional fund.
While the price in the market is higher, there is a demand.
“Perhaps the grain will be put up for auction, after the New year,” he said at yesterday’s press conference.
The Minister reminded that this year the crop of agricultural crops for the 2013 harvest amounted to 3.1 million hectares, including an area of cereals - 1.7 million hectares, which is 3.3% more than last year.
550 thousand hectares were sifted for the 2014 harvest (85 thousand hectares more than in 2012).
Increased areas for winter wheat and triticale, rye remained at the same level.
In the bases of the Ministry of internal Affairs there is no group “Brotherly Circle”, which in the United States ranked leps
In the databases of Russian security forces of the group “Brotherly Circle”, to which Washington ranked the singer Grigory Leps, does not appear.
As noted “Interfax” in the law enforcement agencies of the Russian Federation, after there were reports in the media about the inclusion of Grigory Leps by the U.S. Department of the Treasury on the control lists on suspicion of belonging to the Eurasian criminal syndicate “Brotherly Circle”, all databases were checked, but such a group was not found.
Dissemination of this information contributes to the preservation of the myth of the so-called “Russian mafia”, which allegedly operates abroad, according to law enforcement agencies.
“Even in the very name – “Brotherly Circle”, there is a certain element of mystery, there is an allusion to a secret box.
“All this is very much like a PR campaign”, – said the Agency’s interlocutor.
The U.S. Department of the US Treasury on October 31 announced the inclusion in its checklist on suspicion of belonging to the Eurasian criminal syndicate "Brotherwhee Circle" by Arthur Badalyan, Grigory Lepsvereidze, Vadim Lyalin, Sergei Moskalenko, Yakov Rybalsky and Igor Shlykov.
Persons listed in this list are suspected of links with some Vladislav Leontiev and Gafur Rakhimov, who are considered influential members of criminal groups and have been on U.S. sanctions numbers since February 2012.
According to the American authorities, Grigory Leps "rejoies a courier to deliver money on behalf of Vladislav Leontiev."
Grigory Lepz’s production center refused to comment on U.S. accusations against the singer, calling them “delirium”.
In 2011, U.S. President Barack U.S. Barack Obama conciliated syndica as a “substantial transnational-environmental organized criminal groups” and instructed the Ministry of Finance to “undermine and prevent their global criminal operations.”
The inclusion of a person in the black lists of the American Ministry of Finance entails the freezing of his assets in the United States and a ban on business contacts with him of persons living in the United States.
Scandalous video was caught by the cops
The head of Toronto Rob Ford, known for his scandalous and frank reluctous antics, was caught smoking crack.
The police of the Canadian city said that they have a corresponding video and are ready to start an investigation against the mayor.
He said that his post will not be abandoned, according to CNN.
Information that the authorities have proof of drug use by Rob Ford, appeared on the website of the police of the Toronto police.
The head of the local law enforcement agencies, Bill Blair, held a press conference on this issue.
The sheriff said that he is not authorized to share these shots with the public, but he vouches for its existence.
According to Blair, the comratiatory Rob Ford video was detected during an anti-drug rayake carried out by guards in the summer of 2013.
Previously about the existence of this video has already been painted by the Canadian press, but until recently there was no confirmation.
The mayor himself does not give any comments about this.
He only says that he is not guilty of anything and is not going to resign.
The video discovered by the police is one of the proverrities in the 35-year-old friend of Ford Alexander Lisi, who is accused of trading light drugs, extinguishing, obtaining illegal proceeds, as well as criminal collusion.
Distinctually, Lisi served as the driver of Rob Ford.
Inhabitants of the city have long demanded the resignation of their mayor.
He repeatedly quarreled with journalists, appeared in public in a drunken state, allowed himself racist and sexist statements.
OJSC "Rostovaerainvest" recognized the German company Assmann Beraten + Planen as the winner of the tender at the choice of the general projector of the object.
The abcrèim of the contract is not disclosed.
According to the press service, nine Russian and foreign companies participated in the competition, according to the terms of the tender, the project should be prepared and sent for state examination in the spring of 2014.
The winner will have to design a new passenger terminal of the airport, as well as infrastructural facilities, internal roads and elements for the improvement of the airport complex.
At the first stage of the construction, the internal area of the terminal will be 50 thousand square meters, in the future it is possible to increase it.
According to “Rostovaeroinvest”, the design documentation will take into account the prospects for the development of the airport complex: by 2025 the terminal will be able to serve about 5 million passengers, and by 2035 - 6 million passengers.
At the time of summarizing the results of the tender, an architectural concept of the Yuzhny airport complex was determined, which was developed by Twelve Architects.
The project of the main terminal building embodies the idea of an air bridge between Rostov-on-Don and other cities of the world.
Assmann Beraten + Planen has experience in the implementation of large-scale projects, the company has designed terminals C and E Sheremetyevo International airport and a new auroria complex at KNevichi international airport in Vladivostok.
The Yuzhny international airport complex will be built in the Aksai district of the Rostov region and will replace the existing Rostov airport, which will be closed and integrated into urban development.
The beginning of the construction of the airport complex is scheduled for 2014, the commissioning of all facilities for 2017.
Politician in Turkey went on a hunger strike against the wall on the border with Syria
In the middle of October, the authorities began the construction of a separating wall in the neighbourhood of Nusaybin in the south-east of Turkey.
local residents and representatives of the pro-Kurd PYD party strongly opposed the construction.
The mayor on the border with the Syrian Turkish city of Nusaibin Ayshe Gökhan went on a hunger strike, protesting the construction of a separating wall on the Turkish-Syrian border, told RIA Novosti in the press service of the party of peace and democracy (PMD) on Friday.
The police repeatedly dismantified the protest demonstrations.
Turkish foreign Minister Muammer Güler first refuted the fact of construction, then said that the wall is being built to ensure the security of the borders.
“The mayor of Nusaibina Aishe Goekhan, a member of PMD, went on a hunger strike, thus turning his protest against the construction of the wall into a deadly struggle,” the party’s press service said in a statement.
The mayor of the mayor of the city believes that the construction of the wall is designed to isolate the Kurdish population of the two countries from each other, the Kurds crossed this border freely for half a century.
“This is an intangible situation with which the Kurds will never agree with,” Aysha Goekhan was quoted as saying by representatives of the party.
According to the press service of the press service, it is planned to hold a rally against the construction of a dividing wall in Nusaibin.
Venezuela will set a foreign exchange rate for tourists
Venezuela will introduce a special exchange rate of its national currency - bolivar - in relation to the dollar for tourists.
This was reported on November 1 by Bloomberg with reference to a government decree.
foreign travelers will be allowed a year to exchange amounts quivalent to ten thousand US dollars.
Venezuela will also allow tourists to smash up to 25 per cent of bolivars purchased at the time of departure.
Concrete rate of bolivar in relation to the dollar will be set at a later date.
In February, Caracas was forced to devalue the local currency of up to 6.3 bolivar per dollar.
However, in the black market one dollar is valued at 57 bolivar.
Since the beginning of the year, the bolivar has lost almost 70 percent of its value.
In September, inflation in Venezuela amounted to almost 50 percent.
The Minister of oil and the vice-president for the economy Raphael Ramirez on October 18 stated that Venezuela does not have plans to devalue the bolivar.
According to unofficial information cited by the agency, Karakas can still decide to depreciate the national currency after the municipal elections in December.
Policies to restrain the prices of products and consumer goods, as well as a high degree of overregulation of the Venezuelan economy led to a shortage of a number of goods and the functioning of the black foreign exchange market.
In the spring of this year the media wrote that there was a lack of toilet paper in Venezuela.
The Director of “Ugra” Andrey Belmach noted that while it is difficult to say how much time it will take to find a new head coach.
This post became vacant after the resignation of Sergei Shepelev.
The resignation occurred only a few hours ago, so to say how much time it will take to the search for a new coach, I'm not ready," Belmach said.
Possibly a day.
It's maybe a month.
We are looking into all possible options.
The priority will be given to a Russian specialist.
I don’t just want to find a coach, but such a person who will work in our club for a few years and will achieve certain results with him.
The Romanian press is outraged by provococative law on mass media
“This is a terrible place, and there is a basis for the question: what can be done not to allow Parliament to destroy the independence of the judicial system in the future?” the newspaper said, calling the law unconstitutional.
"This law is very harsh and punitive, and we reject it," said Cyrus Kamau, managing director of Capital Group's parent company CapitalFM, which owns one of Kenya's most cherished independent radio stations and a news site.
He pointed out that the new media judiciary “alway will always be biased, as it is a continuation of the government”, and restrictions on content and advertising will harm the situation of Kenya in the global economy.
“I hope that the President will listen to us, and we are appealing to him with a request to reject this bill and return it to the deputies,” he said.
According to the newspaper The Star, the new law will essentially allow the government to “take the media with a dead grip”, and The Standard reported that democracy and freedom of speech in Kenya “have received a serious blow”, and criticized the bill as “draconian”.
Removal of the bill is part of the measures taken to strengthen national security after the September attack by Muslim terrorists at the Westgate shopping mall.
The Kenyan media have angered the authorities, broadcasting surveillance footage recordings, where the troops that were sent to the site of the attack allegedly plunder an expensive shopping mall.
The reaction of police chief, David Kimayo, was summoned by two journalists and a media official for interrogation, although the call was lifted after mass media protests.
According to the new law, publishing houses can be penalized in the amount of up to 20 million Kenyan shillings, and individual journalists - up to one million with an additional risk to be "excluded from lists", that is, to receive a ban on obtaining official journalistic accreditation.
The court also has the right to confiscate the offender's property, if the fine has not been paid.
According to the Daily Nation, “Even one penalty is enough to paralyze the work of most FM radio stations.”
She also said that these measures can have a devastating effect on the so-creappable bloggnosphere of Kenya.
Politicians understand that, forcing the media to remain silent, they will be able to do everything they please with impunity.
“No one will ever find out,” Nation journalist Mutum Matthew wrote, chasing the Kenyan media as a key source of restraining and balancing forces in social life.
Politicians provided for themselves will ruin the country and bring us back to hunting and collecting,” he wrote.
Kenya legislators have been a target of public wretage in the past.
In May, they voted for the abolition of the reductions imposed by the National Salary Commission, and the restoration of the size of their huge salary, amounting to about 532 thousand shillings per month, tax-exclusive - is one of the tallest in the world.
