what the construction of TPU will lead to in Moscow
Every year the capital authorities promise to equip more and more transport and interfering units (TPUs).
Until 2020 it is planned to put into operation 255 TPUs.
What the project actually turns out, our correspondent understood.
A couple of months ago at the metro "Smolenskaya" Arbatsko-Pokrovskaya line there was a construction fence.
The inscription stated that there was an arranging a transport and interfering node.
all this was very strange, because next to Smolensk no land transport does not stop and, therefore, it is impossible to switch to it.
To get to the nearest trolleybus stop on the Garden Ring, you need to overcome about 130 meter, including a ground passage through Karmanitsky Lane.
Smolenskaya is almost completely finished now.
Floral stalk has vanished off, the stand for newspapers was dismantled, and the asphalt before the entrance was replaced with paving stones.
That's the entire transport hub.
Transport and interchange nodals are flat and capital - the press service of the capital's Department of transport is explained in the press service of the Moscow Department of Transport.
There's no petty TPU yet.
And profense involves the construction of parking lots, the withdrawal of retail facilities that interfering the movement of passengers, the creation of small architectural forms and landscaping.
In fact, flat TPUs are even engaged noted by transport workers, but by professional well-builders from the department of overhaul of the city of Moscow.
The transport hub - this is not necessarily a complex design, "explains Mikhail Blinkin, Director of the Institute of Transport and Transport Policies of the Graduate School of Economics.
Sometimes there is enough a roof over the head and a pillar, noticing about the time of arrival of the transport.
Here, for example, the Yasenevo subway has recently opened quite a full-fledged flat interchange junction.
Let without canopies, but with intercepting parking lots and pillar, indicating when the bus arrives.
But in the pursuit of quantity, the officials write in the TPU everything that gets.
Back in 2011, the mayor’s office was planned to be able to build 151 knacks, of which 59 with capital construction.
Now in the plans until 2020 there are as much as 255 TPUs.
One and a half of them promise to hand over again this year.
Although in the city there is a program for the development of TPU, there are no qualitative criteria - says Alexander Morozov, the co-chairman of the public organization "City and transport".
They are reported on the number of objects, but the quality of the transfer on each of them often deteriorates.
Criteria, according to the expert, there should be only two: first - a decrease in the time of transplantation, and the second - convenience.
First of all, the opportunity to change the type of transport without going out in the rain.
In Moscow when arranging a TPU sometimes leaves exactly the opposite.
Blind example of the VDNH subway.
Earlier, commuter buses from the Yaroslavl highway came to the square in front of the main entrance to VVC.
Now their stops were transferred to the opposite side of Yaroslavka to Cosmonaut Street.
Further from the metro, much further away from the monorail, but closer to residential buildings.
It is for nothing that the residents absolutely did not want the bus station under the windows and complained to all possible instances.
With capital TPU in Moscow somehow immediately did not start.
The first of them began to be built five years ago near the subway "Planternaya".
The project was intended to become exemplary.
And it really turned out to be a sample of how an interchange node donated to investors turns into a banal shopping mall.
No, here there are platforms for buses, a canopy, so you don't go from the subway in the rain, and three parking floors.
However, Khimki trolleybuses number 202 and NO203 in the Moscow TPU did not give places fundamentally.
They were pushed as strangers away from the subway.
There’s a lot of room for trade.
There are only 32 store clothes, and in general there is almost everything - from pet goods to a car showroom.
Well, in fact, suddenly which of the passengers of the bus will need to buy a new car on the road?
We, when they are building a capital TPU, for some reason it always turns out a shopping center.
Recently, the situation has reached its logical conclusion, when part of the parking lot decided to give to the market.
Now on the third floor TPU "Planernaya" there is brulled trade among the parking spaces marked on the floor.
Vegetables, spices, Chinese jeans, non-TRussian speech and security guards, viscously looking at our photographer.
The interchange node finally turned into a bazaar.
The fact is that before the subway "Planner" there was a market, but it was demolished.
And in the prefecture, the merchants were spared and put on an intercepting parking of an interchange node.
It’s because of the high prices, it’s always uneased.
The funniest thing that the market was demolished in order to build in its pillar ... a new flat TPU.
It's such a castling.
At the Kaluga subway, the distance of the approach from the lobby of the metro to the bus was 50 meters, - says Alexander Morozov.
After the construction of a shopping mall, allegedly TPU, the distance increased up to 170 meters.
In order to get on the bus, it is necessary to pass through the entire shopping machination center.
After 22 o'clock, when it is closed, you have to go around it in the open air.
However, the structures on the "Planned" and "Kaluga" will soon seem like floss.
In the middle of September, the town-planning and land commission of the City Hall approved the planning solutions for the first eight capital TPUs.
Four of them will be 25-storey, not counting two or three underground tiers.
The main monster will grow near the Tushino subway, it will be 418.7 thousand square meter square meter.
Representatives of the Directorate of railway stations of Russian Railways, responsible for the construction of TPU near the subway, have already told reporters: in future high-rhundred-eyed high-rise buildings there will be shops, hotels and apartments.
At the same time, officials assure that multi-tiered parking will take from a third to half the area.
Let's take "national" garages for example.
For example, the garage for 258 cars, which was recently plucked on an International street, has an area of 8015 square meter.
So, for parking for 2.6 thousand cars, "Petrov-Razumovskaya" you will need about 80 thousand "squares".
This is less than one-a-a-three of the flies that they are going to build.
Let one or two floins go to all sorts of aprons for the buses.
Remains at least 150 thousand square meters of commercial real estate.
And for a moment, it's almost just two GUMs.
If the capital TPU at the stations and the stations are built by railway workers, the rest of the sites will be mastered by the metro.
They also promised that there will be a lot of “objects of functional purposes”, including hotels, offices and even gyms.
By the way, in the Department of property of the city of Moscow recently told reporters that they are developing a draft resolution according to which investors will be able to appeal to officials to directly.
There are no competitions.
Therefore, they say that transport issues for the city is a priority.
An ideal TPU - for example, the station "Garvard" in Boston or "Spamain" in Toronto, - Alexander Morozov is sure.
There, trolleybuses and trams go underground to the level of the subway and the distance from the subway wagon to the tram is only 50 meters without going out.
There's no extra trade around.
But the Moscow officials are at an extreme.
Either let's not build anything, or we'll kill 25 floors with offices and apartments.
Eser Proposes Equating Extremism Anxiety Anxiety of Patriotic Feelings
To legislatively defend the patriotic feelings of citizens from provocations and insults directed against Russia “Fair Russia” suggests equating an aggravation of patriotic feelings to extremist activity and punish five years in prison during this.
According to the Izvestia newspaper, such amendments to the legislation, prepared by the deputy representative of the Duma Committee on energy Oleg Mikheev, have already been sent to obtain an opinion to the Supreme court and the government.
According to the patriotic feelings of the citizens, the author of the amendments proposes to understand the emotional connection of a person with a citizen of which he is, characterized by a love of love to this country, a responsible attitude to its fate, respect for its history and culture.
As Mikheev points out, in domestic legislation there are sanctions for abusing the formal signs of state power - a flag and coat of arms.
At the same time, according to the parliamentarian, the defense of the Russians, whose feelings can be touched by an aggravation of state symbols and other manifestations of disreprudence towards our country, is not sufficiently worked out in Russian legislation.
As an example, he clarifies the discussions undeveloped annually on Victory Day, when some media persons allow themselves to call into question the heroic feat of the people of the U.S. people in the fight against the fascists.
On the eve eve of the main national holiday - Victory's Victory Day on May 9 - a real bacchanalia is unfolding every year.
Implementing wit and "alternative look" of history, some publicists come to reasoning about the fact that, it's a prying point, what a pity the cultural Germans did not conquer the Wild Soviet Union!
I consider this absolutely inadmissible in the country, where pride in history remains the main “spiritual coffensive” of the nation,” Oleg Mikheev resuscitrated.
In addition, according to Mikheev, there are much more patriotic-minded people in Russia than religious ones, but at the same time the law penalize insults the feelings of the believers, and you can insult patriotic feelings almost with impunity.
In the opinion of the MP, it is Necessary to equate an aggravation of patriotic feelings to extremist activity and prescribe the corresponding punishment in article 282 of the Criminal Code.
The bill provides for the punishment for insulting the patriotic feelings: from a 100-thousandth fine to 5-Year-Year Detention.
