Medvedev Expects SSJ-100 Aircraft to Be Offered
Russia expects that after confiscation in the markets of Latin America and Asia, Superjet 100 aircraft will also be supplied to Europe.
“We are counting on the fact that in total we will receive such such agreements for more than 170 specimens of such aircraft”, – quotes “Interfax” the words of the Prime Minister of Russia Dmitry Medvedev, he said at a press conference with French Prime Minister Jean-Marc Ayrault.
The head of the Russian government noted that serious cooperation has been established with French counterparts, since this is a joint project.
Today we have discussed a number of financial issues that are related to insurance, but we hope that after this aircraft strengthens in Latin American markets and the Asia-Tracial region, it will also be supplied to our partners in Europe.
