Power engineers of Dnipropetrovsk began a unique program to save ... nest storks
In antiquity, in order to crook the storks, the villagers on a high pillar installed a wheel from a cart, and the heavi n nescess was a good nest kept on it.
Such special pillars have not been installed for a long time, so the storks chose the pillars of power lines - intertwined branches are relied on wires, thanks to which the aistic house is reliable.
Grandmother Anya, near the house of which in the village of Ivanovka Petrikovsky district for twenty years already has been inhabited for twenty years, she began to reprize how the nest settles, despite all the diligence of its inhabitants.
The birds put new tweezers from above, and the bottom layer has already drifted between the wires, it's about to collapse.
Of course, it is a pitiful family of storks who every year nested at the farmstead, withdrew and fed three or four chicks during the summer, but you do not want to stay without light.
As soon as the birds fed away to warm regions, grandmother Anya called the Tsarichanskaya RES, which owns the porpoise.
I didn’t even think they’d responsive so quickly.
When our specialists came to Ivanovka, they were surprised that the nint is still still holding, - Sergey Berezovsky, the technical director of DTEK "Dneproblenergo".
corrosion on the wires, which turned out to be, in fact already inside the socket, weighing 150 - 200 kilograms, corrosion has begun.
At any moment, the birds could have died from an electrical discharge.
And the local residents risked to be left without light due to damage to the wires.
Therefore, linear monders have launched an operation to save the nest, and not for the first time in our practice.
Were helped by ornithologists from the Dnipropetrovsk National University, who have developed a nest relocating scheme.
They also conducted training for employees of the district networks.
Famous Dnipropetrovsk ornithologist Alexander Ponomarenko consulted power engineers at all stages of the reconstruction of nests.
To begin with, it was estimated that there are more than 50 stork “apartments”.
For their reconstruction were brewed special metal platforms resembling a funnel.
The basis was splashed with willow branches, and then the old nest was transferred there.
According to connoisseurs, it is enough to lay the old branches as a basis, so that the birds recognize the nest and return to it.
The storks will then rebuild their homes themselves.
A month ago in the village of Peschanka Novomosmoskovskiy district was renovated the first nest.
A new reinforced concrete pillar was placed next to an electric porpox and a platform with an old, already inhabited nest was placed on it.
The whole operation cost the power engineers nine thousand hryvnia.
And in the other day the same nobility took place in the village of Ivanovka Petrikivskyi district in the farmstead of grandmother Ani.
Here the platform is fixed in the same place, only raised above the wires.
Ornithologists are sure that cautious, conservative birds will not even notice in the spring that their "apartment" has been overhauled.
Until the end of the second of the year the same reconstruction awaits four more nests in Pokrovsky and Tsarichansky districts of Dnepropetrovsk region.
By the way, while some save rare birds, others mercilessly kill.
In the other day the whole region flew a sad message - in the village of Ust-Kamenka of the Apostolovsky district, on the day of the opening of the hunt for pheasants, poachers for the sake of entertainment shot a swan family who lived on a local pond.
Noble-natal birds were not at all afraid of people - locals fed them and did not offend them.
When the villagers, having heard the shots, rushed to the pond, four benequal benefactors already lay dead on the water.
Now Employees of the Apostol district police department are finding out who shot the birds listed in the Red Book.
"Russian march" is becoming more popular
November 4, the Day of National Unity will be held in Moscow, the “Russian March” agreed with the mayor’s office will be held in Moscow.
According to the Levada-Center survey, the support of "Russian marches" is growing - already 40% of citizens in varying degrees approve the idea of their holding.
According to “Lyvada-Center”, 40% of citizens in varying degrees approve of holding “Russian marches”: of which 11% belong to such shares are definitely positive and 29% “rather positive”.
The popularity of the idea of "Russian marches" is gradually growing - in 2006 these actions were welcomed only by 14% of Russians, and in December 2010, twice as many of the citizens (28% have already supported such events).
“Definitely Negularly Negligedly, only 7% of Russians” apply to the “Russian Margins”, “rather Negligedly Negularly” – 19%.
Another 35% could not articulate their attitude to this action.
This year the mayor’s office of Moscow agreed to hold the “Russian march” numbering up to 15 thousand people in Lublin, the head of the Department of security of the capital Alexei Mayorov said today.
This action of nationalists takes place every year on the Day of National Unity since 2005.
To the question of sociologists “Did you hear about the fact that on November 4 in Russia held “Russian marches” under the slogans of defending the rights of Russians in Russia? three quarters (75%) of citizens responded negatively.
Now about this action knows only one in five Russians (20%).
It is noteworthy that in December 2010, almost a third of citizens (31%) were heard about the “Russian marches”.
Recall that three years ago on December 11 on Manezhnaya Square there was a spontaneous rally of nationalists, which turned into mass turmoil.
“Levada-center” also asked the Russians about what holiday is celebrated on November 4.
For two years, the number of those who know the correct answer has increased from 41% to 49%.
However, to celebrate this holiday is collected by only 15% of citizens.
Approroximately the same number (17%) intend to celebrate the Day of the October Revolution on November 7.
The majority of citizens (62%) are not going to celebrate any of these holidays.
How the mayor’s office of Moscow agreed “Russian march” in Lublin
October 28, the capital authorities agreed to hold the “Russian March” on November 4 in Lublin.
This was announced by the leader of the association “Russians”, the organizer of the march Dmitry Demushkin.
In addition to the march in Lublin on the Day of National Unity there will be a rally and a rock-concert of Kolovrat, also agreed with the authorities.
How was the "Russian March-2012"
On the Day of National Unity in 2012, the nationalists marched from the Yakikan embernium to the Central House of Artists, where a rally took place.
The organizers estimated the number of participants in 20 thousand people, the interior Ministry called the figure of 6 thousand.
The election headquarters of the election of Obama considered the exclusion of Biden in favor of Hillary Clinton
According to The New York Times, closest advisers to President Barack-Obtobe were gigantly considering replacing Vice-President Joe Bieden with Hillary Clinton’s candidacy in the 2012 electoral list.
This discovery is the brightest sensation of Marc Halperin and John Hilemén’s upcoming book about the 2012 campaign “Stacks are Doubled: The Gaming Has Changed in 2012”.
The Times received a speciance of a forthcoming book and reported on Thursday evening that the president's closest aides conducted “large-scale studies in focus groups and public opinion polls at the end of 2011” to assess whether Biden’s graduation could help raise fading hopes for Obama’s re-eligence.
According to political columnist The Times Jonathan Martin, the book gives a detailed description of an attempt by high-ranking officials of the election headquarters and the White House, namely the former head of the White house administration, Bill Daley, to assess what effect the appointment of former Secretary of State of Clinton as a vice-president.
Possible replacement was a mystery, carefully guarded at the Chicago pre-election headquarters and the Oval Office.
“Only the six closest advisers of the President – including Daley, the former head of the Obama campaign Jim Messina and former senior advisers of the White House, David Axelrod and David Pluff – knew the replacement was being considered.
Bets doubling says Daley was initiating an attempt to replace Biden despite their “close personal relationships,” but end up abandoning that move when their data showed adding Clinton to the electoral list wouldn’t “improportionate Obama’s chances.”
In an interview with Martin Daly confirmed that the administration was really considering replacing Biden Clinton.
“I’ve been actively advocivating to address a lot of things and it was one of them,” Daley said.
You have to keep in mind that at that moment the president was terrified, so we thought: “Oh my God, what are we going to do?”
Although Daley described the study as a “necessary check”, Martin told CNN spokesman Anderson Couper that the pre-election headquarters has invested quite a lot in the study of whether this step will bring dividends on the vote.
“Executive headquarters don’t spend such amounts of money on surveys and focus groups if they don’t consider something seriously,” Martin said in the AK 360 program.
Unclear, however, did Obama know that his team was studying the possibility of a resurgence.
Martin told CNN that he asked Daley if his boss knew about a possible shuffling.
Although Daley said that he doesn’t think the president was “rettaining” a possible replacement, the former head of the administration admitted “perhaps,” Obama knew.
Martin added that the “Stages are doubled” do not give a clear answer to the question of whether political sensing results have come to the Obama table.
Couper asked Martin if he seriously believed that Obama did not know the possibility of removing Biden from the electoral list.
“Maybe,” Martin replied.
