Due to the new rules imposed by Russian customs, for almost a week on the border with Russia in the queue there are hundreds of trucks in the queue.
Today Donetsk officials promised to provide drivers with drinking water
Hundreds of trucks have accumulated at the border points at the entrance to Russia.
Such a situation has arisen due to a change in the rules of customs clearance of goods.
Ukrainian border guards and customs officers confirm: the queue is created by the Russian side, which has not warned in advance about the innovation.
Since October 28, the customs authorities of Russia began to apply additional measures to guarantee the delivery of goods, – said the deputy head of the Eastern customs Vladimir Denisov.
The document of the new model applies in countries that have acceded to the convention on international transport.
The checkpoints operate in an amplified mode.
Correspondent "FACTS" visited the border and communicated with far-fighters who turned out to be held hostages of the situation.
Prices are growing every day, as well as the queue of trucks at the Novoazovssk check-in.
Trucks stand in several rallies, stretching about two kilometers.
The Novoazovska-Vezvelo-Voznesenka customs terminal provides one of the most important transport directions from the south of Ukraine along the international motorway.
From here the goods are sent to the Stavropol Krai of Russia, Kazakhstan, Georgia, Armenia.
On Sunday until mid-afternoon was still allowed, and then these rules were introduced - complains Trucker Aleksey Golyanev (in the photo), who is carrying a cargo from Turkey through Russia to Kazakhstan and has been sleeping in his own car for almost a week.
According to the new rules in order to cross the border, I need an additional package of documents and payment for cargo insurance.
The amount depends on the cost of the goods and the distance at which it is carried.
The minimum insured - 4.5-5 thousand rubles (about 1100−1300 hryvnia).
Those who go close (say to Georgia, Armenia) with a cargo cost of up to 50 thousand dollars, pay somewhere 15 thousand rubles (3800 hryvnias) and pass.
And the others are stranded - after all, no one has such a big money with himself!
You imagine, if the driver is carrying a cargo in the amount of only four thousand dollars, but as soon as in Moscow, he needs 90 thousand rubles (almost 23 thousand hryvnia) to pay for the transit!
Condolences for Survival at the Border - - lament truckers, who have settled eat near their own cars.
In border shops and café is already too expensive, but such prices as here, we have not met anywhere!
Sellers orientated them quickly: 15 hryvnia is a loaf, seven hryvnia - a glass of coffee, 25 hryvnia - a plate of soup.
There's a coffee shop alone.
There is no toilet.
In the step of the steppe we sleep, we also go to the toilet.
Don't wash, don't shave...
I can not get out of the car for a week, my wife on the road prepared everything on my way.
A week I will stretch out, - consolidates another trucker Viktor Skotarenko consolidates himself.
Will it get to my car for a week's queue?
Why do you have one and a half liters of vodka? - We are interested in a single border shop.
There are 11 and 15 hryvnia.
What, the bottle is croused or water installed on the silver?
We've got a café, not a shop.
"Take, while there's something else," the saleswoman retorts.
After the situation began to be covered in the media, the authorities of the region turned to the distabilistic situation of Ukrainian drivers.
The leadership of Amvrosiyevskaya and Novoazovsky district state administrations received an instruction to provide everyone who is idle in the queue on the Ukrainian-Russian border with drinking water, - said Sergey Dergunov, acting chairman of the Donetsk regional state administration.
Ambulance brigades are on duty at the checkpoint.
Also, for the comfort of people, toiletries will be installed.
According to the official, the problem associated with queues will be solved in the next few days.
According to the press service of the Donetsk regional state administration, as of on October 31, 32 and 68 cars were ippled at Uspenka and Novoazovsk border checkpoints.
"FACTS" will monitor the development of the situation.
Vilnius Suspects Moscow of Attempt to Slander the Lithuanian-Lithuanian
Russia intends to carry out information provocations against high-ranking officials of Lithuania and the Eastern Partnership countries - such a statement was made by the BNS agency in the Department of State Security of the Republika BC.
Information about this is published on the portal DELFI.
According to the report, in particular, Moscow is going to “incriminate” the President of Lithuania Dala Grybauskaite and publish falsified documents allegedly found in the Russian State Archive, which concern the facts from the biography of the Lithuanian leader.
According to the special service, the preparation of the information attack is carried out by the department of analysis of the public processes of managing the presidential administration of the President of Russia on inter-regional and cultural relations with foreign countries.
The structure is headed by Yevgeny Umereenkov, who repeatedly visited Lithuania and took part in the congress of the Lithuanian People's Party.
Also, the participant of the operation allegedly is an employee of the department V. Smirnov.
Smirnov under the guise of scientific work until the end of 2012 regularly came to Lithuania and was in contact with local politicians, political analysts and representatives of the media.
Now Smirnova is forbidden to enter the territory of the country.
On the eve of the President of Lithuania Grybauskaite said that she is aware of the impending informattak.
In its opinion, the main reason is the successful presidency of the Council of the European Union and the “spiritual desire for energy independence”
The Lithuanian leader has previously repeatedly criticized the actions of the Russian authorities.
So she stated that in the Krem to the Kremlin to Lithuania are “sufficiently respectable”.
In addition, Grybauskaite accused the President of the Russian Federation Vladimir Putin of nominating “is only demands” to Lithuania.
We will remind, in September, Rospotrebnadzor stopped the import of Lithuanian “milk” to Russia.
IT was reported that the quality of products does not meet sanity and epidemiological standards.
Then the leader of Lithuania said that if Russia does not lift the ban, the country's government should prepare an appeal to the WTO.
