Tripody  Denies That Obeid Is Influenced
Joe Tripodi’s former New South Wel-Hungary Secretary of Detective will be involved in an investigation by an anti-corrupt oversight body in this state.
The former Minister of New South Welmber Joe Tripodi refutes the introduction of changes in the procedure for the rental of seaweather objects at the request of his political mentor Eddie Obeid, who secretly owned shares in three real estate objects on state land.
The Independent irritus Commission (ICAC) on Friday expanded its investigation of whether Mr Obeyd lobbied from several state ministers to extend lease agreements for Serkyulár K, where the Obeid family owns two restaurants and cafocats, without passing the tender after their expiration in August 2005.
She is now investigating allegations that Mr. Tripodi was acquitted of Mr. Obeyd's clandestine participation in the real estate objects, after testimonies given by the former deputy chief of office, Mr. Tripodi Lynn Eshpool on Thursday.
During several years of discussions, which began in 2005, the government insisted that the lease be put forward for an open competition.
