But he denounced that the changes had been carried out at the request of Mr. Obeid, who, according to Mr. Tripodi, strongly advised changes to the government's rental policies.
ICAC transcript of telephone conversations contained conversations in August and September 2007 between Mr. Obeyd, Mr. Tripodi and Steve Dun, a senior official who came to the port ministry after working under Mr. Obeyd in the Fisheries Division.
“Is the issue discussed during these telephone conversations a matter of commercial leasing policy development?” asked Assistant Commissioner Anttoni Weely, Mr. Tripodi.
