Syria has destroyed its means of fabrication of chemical weapons, says the observational group
Syria has destroyed the main equipment for the production of chemical weapons and munomations with toxic gas, an international observatory team said on Thursday, while violent clashes rattled in the north of the country, not far from one object, where toxic substances are believed to be stored.
Also on Thursday, the Syrian group of activists said that more than 120 000 people were killed since the beginning of the civil war almost three years ago.
The statement of the organization for the prohibition of chemical weapons was made one day before
The deadline on November 1, established by this organization based in The Hague to destroy or “complicate unemployable” all means of production of chemical weapons and mechanisms to confuse chemicals with the receipt of the poison gas and fill them with munition.
Completion of what is essentially the initial stage of destruction is an important milestone in an ambitious cliché that aims to derehend all the chemical weapons of Damascus by the middle of mid-2014.
Destroying the equipment means that Syria can no longer produce new chemical weapons.
Nevertheless, Damascus has yet to start destroying existing weapons and stockpiles.
The country is believed to have about 1000 metric tons of chemicals and weapons, including pulp gas and sarin nerve gas.
