At the same time, the State traffic inspectorate every six months will carry out the monitoring of exams.
If it turns it out that more than 30% of examinations on the theory and more than 20% of the site students do not pass from the first time, such a school will be devoid of privilege for six months.
Technological requirements for circuits, contained in the draft government decree, come into force on November 5, 2014.
The project also contains requirements for learning to drive two-wheeled equipment.
From January 1, 2015, the owners of motorbikes to obtain rights of category A will have to take an exam in urban traffic conditions.
In addition, from May 5, 2014, companies will not be able to employ drivers of foreigners with foreign rights.
Such emplary workers will have to receive Russian rights after passing the exam.
