The head of the head of Gazprom Alexey Miller says that the pipeline in Bulgaria marks a new epoch in the gas sector
The beginning of the construction of the South Stream gas pipeline in Bulgaria marked the launch of one of the largest energy projects in Europe, said the head of Gazprom.
“Today there was a significant event: the construction of the Bulgarian section of the South Stream gas pipeline, the most large-scale and most important project in Europe, began to be built, ”said Alexey Mall Miller, chairman of Gazprom, in a statement on Thursday.
This project is a key element of the energy security of the entire European Continuation.
“Yuzhny stream” is designed to diversify the export routes of Russia through Europe.
The dispute under the contract between Gazprom and its partners in Ukraine, which contains most of Russia's gas destined for Europe, increases the level of risk for conventional routes, officials said.
Millèll stated that a direct connection with Bulgaria, a member of the European Union, means that the geopolitical risks associated with the transit countries have been eliminated “for forever”.
Bolguar consumers will receive gas from South Stream at a reduced price, as soon as in 2015 the entire project begins to work.
Gazprom said that the construction should begin in other countries, located further along the route of the gas pipeline, by the end of the year.
The pipeline’s annual design capacity is 2.2 trillion cubic feet of natural gas.
