Published the call of the Chinese newspaper “client to be reorganized”
The Chinese newspaper, which published on the front page the call for the releasing the liberation of a reporter, should be reorganized, according to the press regulator.
Published in Guangzhou, the newspaper “New Express” made an unexpected public statement with a request for the emancipation of journalist Chen Yongzhou.
But Mr. Chen subsequently confessed on television that he took bribes for writing false articles about a company with a state-owned ownership.
Now “The New Express” must go through a “finally correction of errors”, according to the regulator.
Errivet-correction orders came from Guangdong Press and Publications, Radio, Film and Television.
Preliminary investigation has shown that Yangcheng Evening News Group has published several false reports about Zoomion listed between September 2012 and August 2013.
“The management of the editorial office of “New Express” was disoriented”, – said in a statement of the regulator.
He reports that it was decided to “impose an administrative penalty on Chen Yongzhou in the form of a responsibilities of his reporting license”.
He “allowed an indication of Yangcheng Evening News Group to carry out a complete correction of Errors in the “New Express” and recommended it to conduct an investigation into the situation-affiliated journalists and immediately make changes to the management of the “New Express”.
Mr. Chen has written a number of articles for the “New Express”, in which he claimed financial disruptions in a construction equipment company called Zoomlion.
After he was apprehended, his newspaper published on the front page two calls for his release, stating that she supported his journalistic activities.
But Mr. Chen then appeared on state-of-the-government television with acknowledgment that he published false articles for the money.
“In this case, I have harmed Zoomlion, as well as the entire news media industry and its ability to dedicate public confidence,” he told CCTV.
I did this mainly because I thirsted for money and fame.
I've realized my guilt.
After the confessions of Mr. Chen “The New Express” published an apology on the front page, stating that the newspaper could not properly verify his reports.
