Experts say the practice of embracing confessions in China remains ubiquitous, despite recently adopted amendments to laws prohibiting authorities from coercing anyone to self-registration.
Detected U.S. Tunnel – Mexico for Drug Transplant Equipped, Equipped With Its Own Rail
Found one of the most complex drug smuggling tunnels between the U.S.-Mexico, equipped with proprietary illumination, Ventilation and an electric rail system.
U.S. authorities have described the four-piece tunnel as one of the busiest circulatory moves ever discovered.
This tunnel, whose zigzags make up the length of almost six football fields, connects warehouses near Tijuana (Mexico) and San Diego (USA).
This area is filled with inconspicuous warehouses, which facilitates the hidden load of drugs into trucks.
Tunnel was closed before any drugs were impractically transported through it, as stated by the authorities.
According to court documents, law enforcement officers confiscated eight-and-a-half tons of marijuana and 327 pound of cocaine when a tunnel was found.
Three men, who, according to law enforcement officers, worked as drivers, were charged with storing marijuana and co-coffic for distribution.
In the event of conviction, they will face prison terms ranging from 10 years to life incarceration.
In Nogales, Arizona, smugglers use vast underground drainage canals.
Tunnel is the eighth major ailea discovered in San Diego since 2006.
Several of the largest tunnels have been discovered in Central Mexico after harvesting marijuana in October, which set a difficult task for drug cartels to quickly deliver their product to consumers.
In 2010, the authorities found a passing of about 700 yards, equipped with a rail track that came from the kitchen of one of the houses in Tijuang to two San Diego warehouses.
Retirees increase in Belarus since November
In Belarus since November of this year, pensions have been increasing, BelTA was informed in the Main Department of Responsibilary Retirement of the Ministry of labor and social protection.
From November 1 of this year the average wages of workers in the republic, applied in the previous recalculation of pensions will be carried out, with an increase in its value by 5.4% and a corresponding recalculation of labor pensions in accordance with the decree dated October 21, 2013 No. 478 "On Raising Retirees".
As a recalculation since November, labor old-governors will increase by an average of 5.3%.
The average old-fashioned pension will be Br2 million 295 thousand.
The increase in pensions will affect 2.4 million residents of the republic.
Expenses of the Social Welfare Fund of the Ministry of Labor and Social Welfare of the Ministry of Labor and Social Welfare to pay higher pensions from November this year will be increased by Br274.3 billion for a month.
Simultaneous with the recalculation of labor pensions in November of this year will be recalculated minimum and social pensions, surplikes, increases and surcharges to pensions in connection with an increase in the subsistence minimum on average per capita.
BPM for the period from November 1, 2013 to January 31, 2014 was approved by the government in the amount of Br1 million 47 thousand 530 - 2.1% higher than in force in the period from August 1 to October.
Respectively, by 2.1% from November 1, the size of the minimum labor pensions, social pensions and surcharges will be increased by 2.1% and surcharges to pensions will be increased.
