Nortell Pattrate Suggestions
The group, which owns Thousands of Former Nortel Patent Patent, filed a series of patent lawsuits against mobile phone builders on Thursday, including Google, the price of which it interrupted at Nortel’s bankruptcy auction.
Norttel’s $4.5-budget consortium has filed patent infringement lawsuits with U.S. district courts in Texas against Samsung Electronics Co Ltd, HTC Corp, Huawei and four other companies.
Rockstar is co-occurred by Apple, Microsoft, Blackberry, Ericsson and Sony.
“Mooka is accused of infringuating seven patents.
These Patents Clarify Technologies That Help Comparison search keywords on-the-intermediate online search engines, according to the lawsuit, which is the backbone of Google’s search business.
The representatives of Samsung, Huawei, HTC and Rockstar were unavailable and did not give comments.
Samsung, Huawei and HTC are making phones operating on the Android operating system from Google, which fiercely competes with mobile products from Apple and Microsoft.
In 2011, Google proposed an increment of $900 million for Nortel's patents.
Google several times increased the proposed price, eventually proposing as much as $ 4.4 billion.
Having lost Nortel to Rockstrand consortium Rockstar, Google purchased Motorola Mobility for $12.5 billion, the Motorola Patenity Library in this deal partially determined.
“Despite an unsuccessful attempt to purchase patents at auction that are the subject of a lawsuit, Google has broken and continues to infringuate them,” the lawsuit reads.
Rockstar seeks an increased payment of damages from Google, as it argues that the infringement of patent entourage by Google is intentional, according to the claim.
The first freely-elected president is sworn in
Mohamed Morsi is sworn an oath, but the day of his celebration is unlikely to mark an end to a political struggle in Egypt.
Islamist Mohamed Morsi promised “new Egypt” when he swore an oath, becoming the first freely-elected president, replacing Hosni Mubarak, who was overthrown 16 months.
At his inauguration, Morsi’s Supreme Constitutional Judgment also became the first freely-received Islamist president of the Arab world and the fifth head of state in Egypt after terminating the monarchy about 60 years.
He sworn an oath before 18 judges in black robes in a courthouse on the banks of the Nile, built in the style of an ancient Egyptian temple.
“We are striving for a better future, the new Egypt and the second republic,” Morsi said during a ceremony broadcast live on state-of-monetory.
“The Egyptian people today laid the foundations for a new life – absolute freedom, genuine democracy and stability,” said Morsi, a 60-Year-Old-English engineer with an American education from the “Muslim Brotherflesniers”, a fundamentalist group that most out of the age of 84 years of its expiration was an unleavened organization that served as a target for the harsh actions of successive governments.
Hundreds of soldiers and co-peers were being guarded when Morsi arrived with a small cortege shortly after 11 a.m.
Only a few hundred supporters gathered outside the courthouse to greet the new president, and, unlike Mubarak’s presidential pompomp, the movement was stopped only for a short time to miss his convoy on a usually busy road connecting the city center with the southern suburbs.
Although Morsi was ridiculed as an unchariscient “reserve wheel,” his personal prestige has grown sharply from the moment of his victory and Friday’s speech, in which he tried to present himself as a candidate not only of the Islamists, but also for all those who want to bring to an occupy the work of the uprising of 2011 against an authoritarian Mubarak.
“Egypt today is a civil, national, constitutional and modern state,” Morsi, dressed in a blue business suit with a red tie, judges in a wooden-covered hall where he sworn oath.
Morsi later went to the University of Cairo, where he had to deliver his inaugural speech.
He was given an official reception with an army orchestra, performing the national anthem, during which he stood on the rack “Multerly”.
Feld Marshal Hussein Tantawi was present.
His arrival was greeted with the slogan “Army and the people – one hand”, which chanted hundreds of those gathered in the main plenipotentiary of the university.
Founded in 1908 as a bulwark of secular education, the Cairo University in the 1970-ies became a bulwark of Islamist student groups.
Morsi was sworn a symbolic oath on Friday in Tahrir Square, where an influencing Mubarak’s authoritarian rule last year and pledged to retake the powers of the president, which his position was devoured by a military council that took matters from the ousted leader.
But by agreeing to accept an official oath before the court, and not before the Parliament, as is customary, he fulfills the will of the military, and this is a sign that the struggle for power will continue.
Morsi Speech in Tahrir Square was filled with theatrical populist gestures.
The next meeting of the Association of Mechanical Assists of the Tyumen region was held on the basis of the Yalutorovsky Automobile Plant.
As part of the event, a presentation of a new line for the production of electric welded steel pipes took place.
As the commercial Director of the company Denis Gribanov, in 2011, with the appearance of a new owner, a marketing research was carried out to study the sales market of steel structures in the Tyumen region.
It turned out that the region consumes more than 50 thousand tons of electric welded pipes per month.
After this, it was decided to change the profile of the plant and the installation of equipment for their production.
Already this year, more than 7 thousand tons of manufactured products have been shipped.
investments in the plant accounted for more than 120 million roubles, Denis Grybanov said.
In October launched a new camp, which allows you to increase the assortment.
The plant produces both a small profile of the pipe, which is used for a greenhouse, small forms of construction and in the furniture industry, as well as a large - for the construction industry.
We plan to reach the level of production of 50 thousand tons of products per year, which will be about 10 percent of its consumption in the Tyumen region.
Despite the transition to a different type of activity, the number of employees of the enterprise has not decreased - now it is 157 people, in the plans for the purchase of a new equipment - an increase in the staff by more than 50 employees.
Reconnaissance of cadres is carried out at the enterprise, and the necessary specialists are selected from already available.
Next year, it is planned to introduce a new longitudinal cutting unit of up to five-millimeter steel thickness, which will reduce the cost of production, as well as another station, with a pipe production speed of up to 47 meters per minute.
By the end of 2014, the enterprise is going to master the production of pipes, which are used in housing and communal.
The management of the enterprise puts the task of closing up to 70 percent the needs of the Tyumen region for these products.
Leonid Ostolumov, Deputy Director of the Investment Politics, addressing the heads of industries, advised to pay more attention to the modernization of machine-growing enterprises.
Forms of state support of the industry are also aimed at this, which include the reimbursement of interest rates on loans for the purchase of new equipment and its leasing costs.
This year it is planned to allocate 150 million rubles for these purposes, two-thirds of this amount has already been spent.
The last commission, which will consider subsidizing agreements, accepts documents from enterprises until November 15.
In addition, the budget is reimbursed for the participation of local producers in international fairs.
For the next year the budget provides funds in the amount of 150 million rubles, which can be used to complicate leasing payments and loans for the purchase of new equipment.
5 million will be allocated for participation in the fairs, $ 3 million for energy saving programs.
They are depreciated up to 72 million rubles for reimbursement of ordered and paid equipment, which is carried out in the south of the Tyumen region for an oil and gas complex.
According to Leonid Ostolumov, in the future this form of support will stop, since the motive for its introduction was the compensation of the mineral extraction tax, which the oil companies paid to the regional budget.
At the present time they do not do so and the subsidies become direct spending obligations of the region.
In this regard, the regional government considers direct support for industrial enterprises, rather than the financing of the oil industry.
The help of the budget will be associated with investment projects, which will be implemented in production.
Many business leaders expressed their concern about the current situation in relations with oil workers.
Subsidiation on the equipment purchased by them is a competitive advantage of the industry of the south of the Tyumen region, and with its cancellation it will be difficult to compete at a price with an average zone of Russia, where a cheaper workforce.
In addition, the issue with the Continuity of the new owner of TNK-VR - Rosneft, which has not yet placed its orders at Tyumen enterprises, is unclear.
The agreement on the implementation of the Uwth project expires in 2013, and there has been no applications for its renewal.
At the present time, the enterprises of the region, which specialize in equipment for the oil and gas sector, are not able to form a portfolio of orders for next year.
An open question remains whether taxes will come from oil produced in the Uvatskyi district in the budget of the region or they will be paid at the place of registration of the new owner of the fields.
Tomich will work 240 hours for an extremist clichka in social networks
The Leninsky district court of Tomsk was sentenced to 240 hours of compulsory work of a resident of the city, who posted on the social network a video of an extremist orientation, told RIA Novosti on Friday the representative of the press service of the regional court.
According to the court of the court, in March 2013, the man posted on his page in the popular social network a video, which is included in the federal list of extremist materials.
A criminal case was initiated against him under the article of the criminal code of the Russian Federation “Acts aimed at inciting hatred and enmity, as well as humiliating the dignity of a person committed public”.
“Leninsky district court considered this case in a special order and found the man guilty of committing the above-mentioned crime, imposing a sentence of 240 hours of compulsory work,” – said the interlocutor of the agency.
She added that the man fully pleaded guilty.
Azarov promised the Ukrainians the collapse of the prices of goods after the signing of the association with the European Union
The Prime Minister of Ukraine Nikolay Azarov is convinced that prices in the country will decrease significantly after the country signs an association agreement with the European Union.
About it he said in the course of communication with the readers of his page on “Facebook”.
I can definitely say that the prices are determined by a large number of factors, among which there are, including customs payments.
So, after the signing of the agreement and the entry into force of the provision on the Free Trade zone, the level of customs duties on imports of goods from the European Union will significantly decrease.
And this will mean that the prices should decrease.
“This applies to the goods that come from EU countries,” Azarov wrote.
As far as other goods are concerned, the influence of the agreement on prices will not be so direct, it will be mediated.
Nevertheless, there shouldn’t be an increase in prices either.
Therefore, there are messages on billboards, which have recently appeared quite a lot in our country that the association with the EU is an increase in prices, it is not quite so, or, more precisely, it is not at the same time.
