In Yekaterinburg, the criminal killed the two sisters and burned their bodies
In Yekaterinburg, the police are searching for a criminal who brutally dealt with two sisters.
After the murder, their bodies were burned.
As reported to the “New region” in the press service of the Ministry of internal Affairs of the Russian Federation in the Sverdlovsk region, on the eve of the day in the Kirovsky district of the Ural capital after extinguishing a fire in a three-room apartment, located in a residential building on Uralskaya Street, found the bodies of two women with signs of violent death.
The identities of the victims were soon identified.
It turned out that this is a sister, one of them - a resident of Yekaterinburg for 44 years, the second - a 33-year-old resident of the Orenburg region.
They rented a blenned apartment a few days ago.
His investigation took under personal control the chief police officer of the region Mikhail Borodin.
The internal affairs bodies are working out various versions of the murder, check the alibetics of previously convicted citizens and persons prone to such acts.
In addition, it is established for what purpose the woman rented an apartment, and where they lived before, what they were doing, with whom they maintained the relationship.
The schools urged to pay more attention to mathematics, spell and grammar
School courses of English Literature will require students to study at least one play of Shekespe, a 19th-century romance, Romantic Poetry, and Contemporary British Literature starting in 1914.
“Subpharmaceutical texts” will also be presented at the exam to encourage a more extensive reading.
The combined course of English Literature and language will be abolished.
From 2015, pupils will be obliged to take a separate pro-procedural examination in the language, with persistent recommendations for the selection of British literature as a separate exam.
Tomorrow, the Department of Education should release new curricula in English and Mathematics - the first subjects subjected to radically reassembly.
It will make changes to other basic items next year.
Separately, THE OFQUAL examination regulatory body will provide a revised secondary school graduating structure, with a new system of assessments and a smaller volume of coursework.
Speech in the summer, the Minister of Educated Michael Gove said that “a broad consensus has been achieved that we have to reform our examination system to regain public confidence,” insisting that the school’s graduations would be “more complex, more ambitious and more stringent.”
Studies show that English schools devote less time to mathematics (116 hours a year, or three hours a week for a quarter) than in most countries.
For comparison - Australian schools give an average of 143 hours a year, and in Singapore, pupils deal about 138 hours.
Although there will not be a formal requirement to devote more time to mathematics in the mathematical schedule, coalition sources said large-explosive mathematician school exams, coupled with an increased coefficient in the ranking table, will likely serve as an stimulus to provide schools with additional training on this subject.
In the tuition plan, more attention will be paid to “ties from real-fashion life”, including financial mathematicians.
