Dmitry Medvedev: the rate of growth of the GDP of the Russian Federation is not enough for the development of the state
Prime Minister Dmitry Dmitry Medvedev considers the growth rate of its GDP insufficient for Russia and I am sure that the situation can be improved by simplifying the conditions of lending to business and changing the structure of the Russian economy, focusing on innovation, Reuters reports.
We planned this year the growth of GDP in the region of 3%, perhaps even a little more.
It’s actually a little less than 2 per cent.
Against the backdrop of a recess in a number of countries of Europe it seems not very bad, but for us this is not enough, because the economic base is not as powerful as in a number of countries in a number of countries, and in order to develop, there must be a higher pace in order to develop.
Now it is very important that Russian companies, Russian business receive normal loans at a normal price - this is the first thing that must necessarily be done," the head of government said.
