“Their only problem is poverty,” Bwelle said.
Because of poverty, they can't enjoy their lives."
Seeing the wretches of his father and so many of his compatriots, Buffaler was determined to do something about it.
Last year, Dr. Jorge Bwelle and his volunteer team performed 700 free operations.
He himself became a doctor and works as a vascular sensing surgeon at Jaunde Central Hospital.
He has also established an uncommercial ASCOVIME organization that organizes trips to the countryside on weekends to provide free medical care.
Since 2008, he and his group of volunteers have provided assistance to almost 32 000 people.
Almost every Friday he and up to another 30 people are stuffed into vans, tie medical entourines to rooftops and go on rough terrain to visit villages in need.
They don't always have good luck.
More than once they had to push the cars through rivers and dirt.
But when they come, they are greeted as real heroes: this is a holiday with songs and dances and the best rooms that local residents can offer.
Free medical care in these villages is really an occasion for the holiday, and Bwelle with his wide smile and boundless energy is more than happier to join the amusement.
For the next morning, the brigade began to receive hundreds of patients.
“We receive 500 people on every trip,” Bwelle said.
They come from around in a radius of 60 kilometers from the village, and they come on foot.
Each of these week-to-sential clinics provides a variety of medical services.
Many people are treated for malaria, Tuberculosis, malnutrition, diabetic, parasites and sexually transmitted diseases.
Others can obtain crutches, donated glasses or free birth certificates – the documents required for the school, which many poor families simply can’t afford.
In the evening the brigade conducts simple operations under local anesthesia.
Surveillances, as a rule, are carried out in a school building, a municipality or in the house; after the procedure, patients get up and go to the postoperative zone to make room for the next person.
Using a generator to illuminate operating and sanit illumination of the equipment, Bovelle and his volunteers are open until the early autumn of Sunday.
This is unbearable pace, but dedication of the brigade usually helps to maintain village musicians.
“They’ve been punching the drums all night so we’re awake and keep working,” Bwelle said.
The brigade members go back to the city on Sunday, tired but proud of their work.
This group, consisting of cavalry doctors and foreign medical students, conducted 700 free operations over the last year, and they know that their assistance can make a lot of importance for those they help.
One person explained that he received a free operation for the treatment of a hernia will allow him to work again.
"This will change the future for me and my family," the man said.
In addition to these weekend-to-recreatellations and work at a hospital, Bowlle also works at night in private medical clinics around Yanda.
It is this second work, according to him, provides 60% of the financing of his non-commercial organization; the remaining funds are covered by private donations.
"I don't even know when he's sleeping," said Katy O'Malley, a second-teacher medical student at the University of Drexel in Philalophilia.
He is always either in the hospital or trying to earn money for the organization so you can continue these campaigns.
For future doctors and nursers like O’Malley coming from the U.S.-Europe to join B’bbele in fulfilling his tasks, it’s an opportunity to practice they’d never get at home.
“We were able to assist operations where we helped remove blood scoops or hold tools for Dr. Bovle,” O'Malley said.
As a second-vesting student, you would never get such an opportunity in America.
Voluntary students usually pay for their fares in Cameroon, often arriving with donated medicines.
But upon arrival in Yanda their meals, transport and tuition are being paid for by Bwell.
"He's a hero, no doubt," O'Malley said.
He gives his life to this organization, his desire to help the people of Cameroon indefinitely.
For Bwell, almost a constant workload is not a difficult test.
Assisting living a happy life for others by fulfilling his father’s promise is what brings him great joy.
"I'm so happy when I'm doing this job," Bwelle said.
I'm thinking about my father.
I hope he sees what I'm doing.
I'm doing this to make people laugh to reduce their pain.
Visit ASCOVIME website and see how you can help.
Snowden Congratulations on Wiring by Merkel
Bundestag Deputy Hans-Christian Strebele met with Edward Snowden.
During the conversation discussed the question of whether Snowden can be questioned as a witness by the General Prosecutor’s office of the Federal Republic of Germany in the case of a possible wiretapping of the German chancellor’s phone with US special facilities.
Snowden expressed his readiness to testify.
The meeting could take place either in Moscow or in Germany.
He has made it clear,” Hans-Christian Strebele said, “belief that he knows a lot.
And despite the Fact that the National Security Agency led by Keith Alexander blocked all his movements, Snowden is ready to come to Germany.
At the outgiment, however, you must first clearly define all the conditions of his arrival.
In the meantime, U.S. legislators are beginning to take action in response to the scandal around U.S. spy programs.
The Senate Reconnaissance Committee yesterday approved a bill that introduces additional restrictions on the activities of the U.S. electronic intelligence agency.
Belarus and Turkey are interested in the development and deepening of relations in all spheres and areas.
The Minister of foreign Affairs of Belarus Volodymyr Maky told reporters at a press conference following a meeting with Turkish Foreign Minister Ahmet Davutoğlu, BELTA correspondent reports.
We are very pleased that our Turkish co-workers and partners at all levels are interested in the development and deepening of Belarusian-Turkish relations in all spheres and areas.
Belarus, for its part, is also interested in this, so we have agreed that the public administration bodies of the two countries will provide ubiquitous assistance and support to entrepreneurs who establish direct trade and economic contacts among themselves, ”said Vladimir Makey.
He stressed that the government of Belarus will create all the necessary conditions for this and provide maximum assistance.
The Minister also said that in Ankara the next 8-th meeting of the Belarusian-Turkey joint intergovernmental economic commission was held, as a result of which a protocol was signed.
The parties have worked out a roadmap of Belarusian-Turkish interaction, which, according to the Belarusian foreign ministry, is aimed at deepening bilateral cooperation in the trade, economic and investment fields, in the spheres of industrial co-operation, transport, agriculture, energy, as well as searching for new forms and areas of cooperation.
“The roulos of the last meeting has been carried out in full, and I am convinced that the current protocol will also be fulfilled, because Belarus and Turkey consider each other as reliable partners,” he said.
The Minister of foreign Affairs of Turkey Ahmet Davutoglu, in turn, said that the foreign Ministers of the two countries decided to further develop mutually beneficial cooperation and implement various projects.
Commodity turnover between Belarus and Turkey, according to the Minister, it is necessary to increase and bring it to an indicator of $ 1 billion.
Also, Turkey is an important partner in the field of investment cooperation, which needs to be further developed, since in this area there is unused potential, he believes.
There has always been very warm relations between our countries, and we hope that in the future they will further strengthen and expand.
And all the necessary conditions will also be created for trade and economic ties for the successful work of Turkish companies in the territory of Belarus and Belarusian enterprises and organizations in Turkey, ”said Ahmet Davutoglu.
U.Am. Refusing His Words on Health
“Thric of President Obama’s stor kilomeuty yesterday backed down relative to his often repeated, unequivocal promise that “if you likes your health insurance plan, you can save it.”
Seeing that hundreds of thousands of people received notifications about the termination of services from their providers, Republicans in recent days criticized the president for misleading U.S. society.
Yesterday, Obama slightly tampered his initial public promise.
“Most people who have health insurance that works can keep it,” he said in a speech in Boston.
Refering to the fact that he called “revitalization in the news” about the termination of services, Obama urged the Americans receiving these notations to look for other variants in the market.
The majority of people will be able to get the best, comprehensive health insurance plans at the same price or even cheaper than they have been projected.
“You will get more favorable conditions,” he said.
The administration said that no one should be astonished that 5% of the population who buy insurance on their own may be forced to change plans, because their coating does not meet the new standards necessary in accordance with the law on affordable medical care.
“Please let me say directly to these Americans: you deserve the best,” Sibelius said in a speech to the Committee on energy and tracing of the House of Representatives in Washington.
Sibelius, which oversees the implementation of the Afford-of-accommodation law, said the launch of an online sales site was “terrifyingly bad” since October.
“I’m upset and annoyed just like everyone else,” she said.
- I really want to restore your trust."
Irlished Sibelius blamed this phrase, which was picked by the microphone behind her, an assistant at yesterday’s house hearings after a heated debate with a member of the House of Representatives Billy Long, a Republican from Missouri, about whether she is obliged to join Obama’s health care program herself.
After more than three Hours of Helter, Long once again urged Sibelius to say why the “architect” of the Affordable Medical Affiliation Act hasn’t volunteered against government-sponsored insurance to purchase a plan through HealthCare.gov, which she now imposes on millions of Americans.
Agency “Rosbalt” was deprived the status of the media for obscene swearing
On October 31, the Moscow City Court decided null and void the license to register the Rosbalt agency.
Roskomnadzor insisted on depriving the agency of media status - for systematic and rude violations of the law on mass media.
During the course of the trial, an unpleasant precedent was created: the court considered it possible to close the media, in fact protruding the publication the right to put forward counter-arguments.
What is "Rosbalt"
CJSC “Information Agency Rosbalt” was established in St. Petersburg in 2000.
In the following years, the agency opened a second head office in Moscow and a number of regional subdivisions.
Also, the agency has representative offices in the countries of the former of the USSR.
Since 2001, "Rosbalt" was developing and functioned as a federal information-analytical agency.
By the middle of the 2000-ies the agency was included in the list of the most recognizable private online media in Russia.
At the same time, "Rosbalt" has always occupies a rather specific niche: the core of the exclusive publications of the agency has compiled (and still compose) notes with reference to sources in law enforcement agencies.
Congratulations about the intimacy of the publication to law enforcement agencies continued throughout the existence of the agency.
Along with the fact that “Rosbalt” had an extensive base of sources in various departments, in favor of such assumptions was the fact that Natalia Chaplina was at the forefront – the wife of Viktor Cherkesov.
At the same time Chaplina's role in the management of Rosbalt is not completely clear: it is most often referred to as the "project manager".
The general director of the agency is Larisa Afonina, the editor-in-Chief - Nikolay Ulyanov.
Recently, "Rosbalt" did not appear in the ratings of the federal mass media - neither in citation, nor in the audience.
In October, the agency ranked 25-th in the rating of attendance of sites of the Russian mass media according to LiveInternet.
According to the same LiveInternet, the average daily audience of rosbalt.ru is about 150 thousand unique visitors (and up to 500 thousand views), the monthly - about three millions of unique visitors.
Among the most popular materials in the last five months - notes about the helplessness of the Kremlin in relations with Ukraine, the death of the soloist group "Kyar and jester", pogroms in the capital's Biryulev.
“Rosbalt” with Roskomznadzor began in July 2013, when amendments came into force to the law on the mass media, which prohibited obscene swearing to journalists.
The Ministry found prohibited vocabulary in two videos published on the agency's website ("Jigit from Krasnodar" and "Pussy Riot desecrated oil gallops").
Subsidiaries are described in a different way.
Roskomnadzdar on the basis of detected videos accused Rosbalt of a gross and systematic violation of the law on the media and appealed to the court with a requirement to retake the license from the agency.
In “Rosbalt” stated that the claims of the Department are illegal: firstly, the videos were not editorial materials, and secondly, the mattress words were disgusted in them, and, in the third place, immediately after warning the videos were removed from the site.
Representatives of the agency appealed the claims of Roskomnadzor in the magistrate's court - and when on October 22, 2013 the Moscow City Court accepted the claim of Roskomznadzor, the consideration of these complaints still continued.
However, already on November 25, the magistrate decided not in favor of “Rosbalt”: the editor-in-chief Nikolay Ulyanov was found guilty of violating the code of administrative offenses and was fined 20 thousand rubles - 10 thousand for each video.
Obviously, this predeceived the outcome of the hearing in the Moscow city court - if you give up the idea that the outcome could be predetermined even earlier.
On October 31, the court decided to invalidate the certificate of registration of “Rosbalt”, actually depriving the agency of media status.
It cannot be said that “Rosbalt” in the course of this confrontation was left alone.
The Agency was supported by the deputies of the state Duma (a statement addressed to the head of Roskomnadzor Alexander Zharov on October 10 was signed by 26 deputies; the document itself was filed at the initiative of the CPRF).
About the illegality of the closure of the publication was stated by the head of the Union of journalists of Russia Vsevolod Bogdanov, the Chairman of the Moscow Union of journalists Pavel Gusev and the head of the presidential Council for human rights Mikhail Fedotov.
Moreover, according to Bogdanov, the Roskomnadzor management even provided him with some guarantees that it will not come before the revocation of a license.
Judgment of “Rosbalt” has shown: under whose jurisdiction it is safer to be the media in Russia today is a big question.
Syria Destroy Chemical Weapons Equipment
Syria has destroyed all claimed chemical weapons production facilities, the Organization for the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons recognized.
This the first stage of dismantling Damascus completed the day before the deadline.
Until November 1, Syria had to destroy industrial and other auxiliary facilities intended for the preparation of communicative substances for use.
Destroyment of pollutants themselves or their chemical components must be completed by mid-2014.
According to the representative of the OPCW, at the present time the poisonous substances are in sealed repositories.
International inspectors went to Syria after more than 1,400 people were killed on the outskirts of Damascus on August 21 in a chemical attack.
The main task of the inspectors did not lose time - in order not to allow the Syrian authorities to produce more chemical weapons - and to destroy the infrastructure to mix chemicals and ammunition equipment.
These production facilities will now be carefully monitored in order not to allow them to be repaired.
The next vein is mid-November: by this time the OPCW and the Syrians should agree on a detailed plan for the destruction of already existing stockpiles of toxic substances.
There are a lot of questions here.
Where are they going to be extinguistrenged?
who will provide the equipment for this?
All Syrian statements will be carefully checked by Western intelligence services.
They are ready to advise the inspectors of new facilities for verification, if there will be grounds to suspect that Damascus is not completely fascinated.
The U.S. believed that the shelling was carried out by regular troops.
Syria and Russia insist that this is the work of Syrian rebels.
The international community demanded from the Syrian leadership - in accordance with the agreement reached with the conciliation of Russia - to destroy or put into a non-performing state all the capacities for the production of projectile shells, toxic gases and fluids and to fill the shells with these substances.
Now, when this stage has passed, the next step should be the destruction of already existing chemical weapons of the Syrian army.
It is assumed that in this Arsene there can be more than 1000 tons of nerve-paralytic poisonous substances, skin-gun mustard gas, and other prohibited chemicals stored in several dozen different places.
To exterminate it, it is necessary that the OPCW and the Syrian authorities first agree on a schedule of action - it takes two weeks for this.
The head of the OPCW field operations Jerry Smith told the BBC that his inspectors “personally monitored the destruction of the equipment.”
“They now don’t have the opportunity to further manufacture or mix chemical weapons,” he said.
In a statement, the OPCW stated that the inspectors visited 21 of the 23 facilities in Syria and became convinced that the plants for the production of projectiles and poisonous substances were either destroyed or unufficiable.
The remaining two objects are too dangerous to conduct an inspection there, according to the document, but the equipment from there was transported and checked by OPCW specialists.
According to Smith, the process of extinguishing the infrastructure for the production of chemical weapons was “principally difficult”, since it had to work in the context of the ongoing conflict.
In the beginning of October, the OPCW received the Nobel Peace Prize, however, according to Smith, there has not yet been a time to celebrating this at the inspectors - they were too busy with work.
John Kerry Says U.S. Espionage Comes Inappropriately Accord
John Kerry has demonstrated a relaxation of the tranquility tavern for U.S. tracking, making an unprecedented acknowledgment that in some cases U.S. espionage has “gained impracticably far.”
The Secretary also admitted that he was guilty, along with Barack Obama, of being “on auto-dpilot” during Edward Snowden’s voluminous expises about NSA espionage.
These leaks of information brought the U.S. government at the center of a diplomatic scandal with their allies.
Speech by video link at an open government conference in London, Kerry said: “There is no doubt that the president and I, as well as other members of the government, actually perceived certain things on auto-dpilot, because such an opportunity has already existed – both during World War II and in the very difficult years of the Cold War and, of course, September 11.
Then, he became the first high-profficial member of the U.S. government who recognized that US espionage went too far, but stressed that no one’s rights had been violated.
He said: “In some cases it has gone inconceivably far away.
And the President is determined to shelf the light of this issue and explain himself to the people, and is now conducting a thorough analysis in order that no one has a sense of abusions.
Assuring you, there is no abusions against innocent people in this process."
Mr. Kerry insisted, however, that the NSA had acted for good intentions and that his surveillance operations saved many lives.
He added: “We are working in a new world where people are ready to blew themselves up.
In the world there is a radical extremism, reluctatious and reluctatable to kill people, to blow people and to attack governments.
And if you were able to intercrete it, stop it before it happens?
In fact, we’ve actually prevented plane plane crashes, building explosions and killing people, because we were able to find out about these plans in advance.”
Meanwhile, U.S. legislators will go to Europe to help resolve issues related to alleged US espionage abroad and to persuade Europeans to continue joint anti-terrorist activities with the U.S., the Senate subcommittee’s chairman on European affairs said on Thursday.
Konnektuit Senator Chris Murphy said he had spoken with members of the European Parliament and others this week and was concerned about their threats to stop participating in anti-terrorist organizations due to frustration over the surveillance conducted by the National Security Agency.
“It’s for U.S. national security interests, it’s really important that the Europeans remain our proponents on our common anti-terrorist efforts,” Murphy’s Democrat, who works for the first term and is chairman of the subcommittee of international relations of the Senate on European affairs, said in an interview from Washington.
“And I’m going to Europe to let them understand that we must continue to cooperate in the fight against terrizzard, despite their wretched things about these NSA programs.”
“Reproach that the NSA has complied with millions of telephone conversation records in Europe has deteriorating relations with some U.S. allies, although the agency’s head said this week was inaccurate and repulsed a misunderstanding of metadata collected by NATO’s allies and shared with the U.S.”
In other exhilarations, documents promulgated by Snowden showed that the NSA was monitoring German Chancellor Angela Machel Merkel's mobile phone, as well as the phones of about 34 other world leaders.
National Intelligence Director James Clapper defended espionage activities against the Allies as necessary and said it's a normal business on both sides.
Against the backdrop, Murphy said that his office will organize a trip of members of the Congress, which is expected to take place this year, and that he hopes that the delegation will include members of both parties and both chambers.
The names of other participating legislators should be announced in the coming days.
According to him, the program of the trip is still at the stage of development.
Although Murphy said that the purpose of the trip is to promote an improvement in the relationship, he said that a certain degree of “harseverity from the best of intentions” will also be manifested.
He said that the European leaders should be honest with their people at what espionage programs they themselves have used for many years.
“While we can change our tracking programs in order to better defend the rights of the Europeans, they also have to accept the fact that we’re not the only ones engaged in intelligence,” Murphy said.
In the mean meantime, Kerry should travel to the Middle East and Poland this weekend to address hostility about U.S. strategy in Syria, Egypt and Iran, as well as U.S. reconnaissance.
In the new compositions of public monitoring commissions will increase the influence of jailers
Today the Council of the Public Chamber (OP) can approve the new composition of public Supervisory commissions in 43 regions of Russia.
If the option put to the vote is adopted, siloviki lobists will increase their influence.
ONC - social structures that control the conditions of detention in places of deprivation of liberty.
The cases of Sergei Magnitsky and Leonid Razvozzhaev, excitement in the penitentiary penal colony - it is through the ONK that most resonant accidents are resolved behind bars.
For the control of the HRC there is a strife between human rights defenders and lobbyists of the security forces.
At the meeting of the OP working group on the Formation of ONC, I proposed to make a criterion for the selection of the experience of human rights activities.
“It was not accepted, and they formed lists without finalizing the criteria,” says Valery Borshchev.
Borshchev - the current Chairman of the Moscow Supervisory Commission and the Association of Independent Observers - an all-Russian structure of human rights defenders dealing with prison problems.
As a deputy of the state Duma from “Yabloko” he has developed a law that regulates the activities of the OPC.
The OP Council should vote for the composition of the PNC in 43 regions of the country.
For 1,800 vacancies claim less than a vaccination, and in Ingushetia and Kabardino-Balkaria competitions could not be organized due to the absence of candidates.
OP promises to organize an additional set for vacant seats.
PMC of Moscow - one of the few commissions with the competition, despite the fact that in the new line-up will be 40 participants instead.
According to Borshcheev, in the current composition of the capital’s commission of 11 human rights defenders and 9 siloviki, and in the option, which is on voting in the ON OP, the ratio changes by 17 to 23.
At the same time, 30 human rights defenders wanted to get to the Moscow commission.
But in the new line-of-compartment can be again a representative of "Combat Brotherhood" Vyacheslav Kalinin.
For three years he was a member of the POCS, but never visited the prisoners.
Borshchev believes that the security forces, after appointing their Chairman of the POC, will be able to make the work of human rights activists unbearable, so human rights activists do not exclude a collective withdrawal from the commission.
In their opinion, the movement of the security forces is coordinated by POC member Anton Tsvetkov, who heads the "Officers of Russia" - an organization defending the interests of law enforcement agencies.
“I don’t eat babies for the backpack,” Anton Tsvetkov told RBC daily.
He denies lobbing the promotion of any estuaries and says that he is not going to prevent human rights defenders from visiting the arrested oppositionists.
According to Tsvetkov, he was not even interested in what list they are currently voting in the OP.
Promulgation of Borshcheven information, he considers a form of pressure.
Possible success of human rights activists is the planned change of leadership of the Chelyabinsk ONC.
Its former leaders will be removed because of last year's Kopedic unlance.
In the public chamber came to the conclusion that the leadership of the local commission ignored the problems of prisoners.
Rostov-on-Dan-Don can move from human rights defenders to law enforcers.
From the new lists "disappeared" the human rights activist-presidor of the local commission, but there was one of his opponents, despite the fact that in May 2013 the Federal Public Chamber excluded him for unethical behavior.
Borshchev considers lists of the Moscow and Rostov commissions “a vengeance for Kopeysk”.
Nadezhda Tolokonnikova’s revelation did not affect Mordovia’s PMC, which is considered a “power”: only one human rights activist wanted to fall into the new line-up, and she did not even accept documents for the competition.
Nikolay Svanidze, a member of the OP board, told RBC daily that he voted against the proposed list, since the situation in Moscow and Rostov-on-Dun resuscitated him.
His position was sent out to other members of the council.
Pavel Gusev, his OP colleague, says that he voted for, since he likes the proposed Moscow list.
Coordination was coordinated by the deputy secretary of OP Vladislav Gryb, who is also an employee of the Federal Penitentiary Research Institute.
The mushroom told RBC daily that he does not consider it correct to dividing the candidates for human rights defenders and siloviki and does not agree with the fact that the chairmen of the commissions have enough authority to interfere with the work of its members.
The mushroom does not undertake to predict the results of the voting of the OP board.
If the proposed list will be rejected today, an alternating option will be put to a vote in the next few days.
An Australian woman appeals against a prison sentence in Thailand
A 21-year-old woman from Sidney, who was sentenced to a 15-a-clock prison on Phuket Island for false allegation that she was attacked by a taxi driver, filed an treasury of a verifius and was bailabbed on bail.
Stevie Rochelle Bamford was initially recognized on June 15 by the Phuke Provincial Court guilty of filing a false bail after reporting to the Thai police that a local taxibider had carried out an attack on Sunday night on June 10, while the other two men were holding her.
However, according to confidence cameras, it was later revealed that she returned safely to her hotel after escalating relations with her Australian boyfriend.
Phuket police interrogated Bamford for two days before she confessed to fabricating this story.
Before the trial, she was detained in local police cameras.
Bamford was Sentenced a 15-a-a-day prison term at a general-regular detention center on the outskirts of Phuketa rather than an adult women's prison.
She is the similating daughter of the Australian League Peter Tanks, who appealed to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs in Canberra for help for his daughter.
The Tanks told the Sides-Sydney Sunday Telegraph that the whole family was “extremely concerned” about the well-being of their daughter and was awaiting her to return to Australia.
“Obviously, it’s been anxious time, but we’re hoping that she will return home safely as soon as possible,” Tanks said.
Bamford filed an appeal against her veripulation and was released on bail of 50 000 baht.
According to reports in Australia, at the present time she spends her vacation in the resort area of Krabi in southern Thailand.
Law sources in Thailand said Bamford is currently representing a local lawyer in Phuket, but has been warned that an appeal could result in a court enlarging her sentencing for up to a two-Year-Year-Year sentence and would force her to serve a term in adult prison.
However, after the recent murder of Australian travel agent, Michelle Smythley Smith in Phuket, Thailand may also seek to restore its blered tourist image, leading to an acquittal.
